  FT["MY-H5877"] = {"id":"MY-H5877","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 42/2018&status=AMENDMENT","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2018年费用（向财政部注册公司）（修正）令","en":"FEES (REGISTRATION OF COMPANIES WITH MINISTRY OF FINANCE) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2018","orig":"FEES (REGISTRATION OF COMPANIES WITH MINISTRY OF FINANCE) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2018","ms":"Perintah Fi (Pendaftaran Syarikat dengan Kementerian Kewangan) (Pindaan) 2018","vi":"Lệnh về Phí (Đăng ký công ty với Bộ Tài chính) (Sửa đổi) năm 2018","th":"คำสั่งค่าธรรมเนียม (การขึ้นทะเบียนบริษัทกับกระทรวงการคลัง) (การแก้ไข) ค.ศ. 2018","id":"Perintah Biaya (Registrasi Perusahaan pada Kementerian Keuangan) (Perubahan) Tahun 2018"},"level":"regulation","category":"02_民商事与经济法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA42","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2018","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\02_民商事与经济法\\2018_P.U.(A)42-2018_FEES (REGISTRATION OF COMPANIES WITH MINISTRY OF FINANCE) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2018.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H5877-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. Perintah ini boleh lah dinamakan Perintah Fi ( Pendaftaran Syarikat dengan\nKementerian Kewangan) (Pindaan) 2018.\n\nPindaan Jadual"}},{"id":"MY-H5877-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Perintah Fi (Pendaf taran Syarikat d engan Kementerian Kewangan) 2017\n[P.U. (A) 30/ 2017] dipinda dalam Jadual dengan memotong butiran 5 dan butir -butir\nyang berhubungan dengannya.\n\nDibuat 15 Januari 2018\n[BPK/ S/K.KEW/PK/MOF/D/65JLD.2 SK.2; PN(PU2)86/XXVI]\n\nDengan Titah Perintah\n\nTAN  SRI  DR.  ALI BIN HAMSA\nSetiausaha Jemaah Menteri\n\n[Akan dibentangkan di Dewan Rakyat menurut seksyen 4 Akta Fi 1951]\n\nFEES ACT 1951\n\nFEES (REGISTRATION OF COMPANIES WITH MINISTRY OF FINANCE)\n(AMENDMENT) ORDER 2018\n\nIN exercise of the power s conferred by section 3 of the Fees Act 1951 [ Act 209 ],\nthe Yang di-Pertuan Agong makes the following order:\n\nCitation"}}],"pack":"my-13"};
  FT["MY-H5878"] = {"id":"MY-H5878","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 42/2019&status=AMENDMENT","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":3,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2019年所得税（豁免）（第7号）2018（修正）令","en":"INCOME TAX (EXEMPTION) (NO. 7) 2018 (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2019","orig":"INCOME TAX (EXEMPTION) (NO. 7) 2018 (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2019","ms":"Perintah Cukai Pendapatan (Pengecualian) (Bilangan 7) 2018 (Pindaan) 2019","vi":"Lệnh về Thuế thu nhập (Miễn trừ) (Số 7) 2018 (Sửa đổi) năm 2019","th":"คำสั่งภาษีเงินได้ (การยกเว้น) (ฉบับที่ 7) 2018 (การแก้ไข) ค.ศ. 2019","id":"Perintah Pajak Penghasilan (Pembebasan) (Nomor 7) 2018 (Perubahan) Tahun 2019"},"level":"regulation","category":"02_民商事与经济法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA42","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2019","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 3 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\02_民商事与经济法\\2019_P.U.(A)42-2019_INCOME TAX (EXEMPTION) (NO. 7) 2018 (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2019.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H5878-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Cukai Pendapatan\n(Pengecualian) (No. 7) 2018 (Pindaan) 2019.\n\n(2) Perintah ini disifatkan telah mula berkuat kuasa mulai\ntahun taksiran 2018.\n\nPindaan perenggan 3"}},{"id":"MY-H5878-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Perintah Cukai Pendapatan (Pengecualian) (No. 7) 20 18 [P.U. (A) 386/2018],\nyang disebut \"Perintah ibu\" dalam Perintah ini, dipinda da lam subperenggan 3 (d)\ndengan memotong perkataan \"yang terletak di tiga negara di luar Malaysia\".\n\nPindaan Jadual 2"}},{"id":"MY-H5878-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"ms":"3. Jadual 2 kepada Perintah ibu dipinda—\n\n(a) dalam Syarat-syarat bagi hab prinsipal yang meny ediakan\nperkhidmatan yang layak  dengan memotong sya rat \"Lokasi\nperkhidmatan yang layak disediakan oleh hab prinsipal kepada syarikat\nrangkaiannya yang salah satu daripada perkhidmatan yang layak\nhendaklah daripada item (a) kluster (1) Jadual 1\" dan butir -butir yang\nberhubungan dengannya; dan\n\n(b) dalam Syarat-syarat bagi hab prinsipal yang menyediakan aktiv iti\nperdagangan yang layak  dengan memotong syarat \"Lokasi aktiviti\nperdagangan yang layak disediakan oleh hab prinsipal kepada syarikat\nrangkaiannya\" dan butir-butir yang berhubungan dengannya.\n\nDibuat 18 Februari 2019\n[Perb.0.3865/73(SJ.133-8); PN(PU2)80/XCIV]\n\nLIM GUAN ENG\nMenteri Kewangan\n\n[Akan dibentangkan di Dewan Rakyat menurut subsek syen 127(4)\nAkta Cukai Pendapatan 1967]\n\nINCOME TAX ACT 1967\n\nINCOME TAX (EXEMPTION) (NO. 7) 2018 (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2019\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by paragraph 127(3) (b) of the\nIncome Tax Act 1967 [Act 53], the Minister makes the following order:\n\nCitation and commencement"}}],"pack":"my-13"};
  FT["MY-H5879"] = {"id":"MY-H5879","coverage":"partial","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 42/2020&status=AMENDMENT","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":5,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2020年联邦道路（私营管理）（通行费征收）（槟城大桥）（修正）令","en":"FEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS) (PENANG BRIDGE) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2020","orig":"FEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS) (PENANG BRIDGE) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2020","ms":"Perintah Jalan Raya Persekutuan (Pengurusan Swasta) (Kutipan Tol) (Jambatan Pulau Pinang) (Pindaan) 2020","vi":"Lệnh về Đường bộ liên bang (Quản lý tư nhân) (Thu phí đường bộ) (Cầu Penang) (Sửa đổi) năm 2020","th":"คำสั่งทางหลวงสหพันธ์ (การบริหารจัดการเอกชน) (การจัดเก็บค่าผ่านทาง) (สะพานปีนัง) (การแก้ไข) ค.ศ. 2020","id":"Perintah Jalan Raya Federal (Pengelolaan Swasta) (Pemungutan Tol) (Jembatan Penang) (Perubahan) Tahun 2020"},"level":"regulation","category":"05_其他及未分类","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA42","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2020","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 7 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\05_其他及未分类\\2020_P.U.(A)42-2020_FEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS) (PENANG BRIDGE) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2020.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H5879-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. Motosikal -"}},{"id":"MY-H5879-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. (a) Motosikal dengan kereta sisi\n\n(b) Kenderaan perniagaan beroda tiga\n\n(c) Kereta termasuk station wagon\n\n5.74"}},{"id":"MY-H5879-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"ms":"3. Van dan bas dengan dua gandar dan empat roda 9.84\n\n3A.\n\n 4A.\n\nLori dengan dua gandar dan empat roda\n\nVan dan bas dengan dua gandar dan lima atau enam roda\n\nLori dengan dua gandar dan lima atau enam roda\n\n12.00\n\n20.50\n\n25.00"}},{"id":"MY-H5879-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"ms":"5. Bas dengan tiga gandar 36.90\n\n5A.\n\nLori dengan tiga gandar\n\nKenderaan dengan empat gandar\n\n45.00\n\n60.00"}},{"id":"MY-H5879-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7"},"text":{"ms":"7. Kenderaan dengan lima gandar atau lebih 75.00\n\nBagi maksud mengira bilangan gandar dan roda sesebuah kenderaan, gandar dan roda\n\nmana-mana treler yang ditarik oleh kenderaan itu hendaklah dikira sebagai sebahagian\n\ndaripada gandar dan roda kenderaan itu.\".\n\nDibuat 31 Januari 2020\n\n[KKR.PUU.110-1/7/20; PN(PU2)426/LXVIII]\n\n BARU BIAN\n\n Menteri Kerja Raya\n\nFEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) ACT 1984\n\nFEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS)\n\n(PENANG BRIDGE) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2020\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 2 of the Federal Roads\n\n(Private Management) Act 1984 [Act 306], the Minister makes the following order:\n\nCitation and commencement\n\n1. (1) This order may be cited as the Federal Roads (Private Management)\n\n(Collection of Tolls) (Penang Bridge) (Amendment) Order 2020.\n\n (2) This Order comes into operation on 1 February 2020.\n\nAmendment of paragraph 2\n\n2. The Federal Roads (Private Management) (Collection of Tolls) (Penang Bridge)\n\nOrder 1995 [P.U. (A) 410/1995], which is referred to as the \"principle Order\" in this\n\nOrder, is amended in subparagraph 2(1) by substituting for the words\n\n\"31 December 2038\" the words \"31 December 2058\".\n\nSubstitution of Second Schedule\n\n3. The principal Order is amended by substituting for the Second Schedule the\n\nfollowing Schedule:\n\n\"SECOND SCHEDULE\n\n[Subparagraph 2(1)]\n\nRATES OF TOLLS FOR THE PERIOD FROM 1 FEBRUARY 2020 TO 31 DECEMBER 2058\n\n (1)\n\n Classes of Vehicles\n\n(2)\n\nToll Payable\n\n(RM)\n\n1. Motorcycles -\n\n2. (a) Motorcycles with sidecars\n\n(b) Commercial vehicles on three wheels\n\n(c) Car including station wagons\n\n5.74\n\n3. Vans and buses with two axles and four wheels 9.84\n\n3A.\n\n 4A.\n\nLorries with two axles and four wheels\n\nVans and buses with two axles and five or six wheels\n\nLorries with two axles and five or six wheels\n\n12.00\n\n20.50\n\n25.00\n\n5. Buses with three axles 36.90\n\n5A.\n\nLorries with three axles\n\nVehicles with four axles\n\n45.00\n\n60.00\n\n7. Vehicles with five axles or more 75.00\n\nFor the purpose of calculating the number of axles and wheels of a vehicle, the axles and\n\nwheels of any trailer towed by the vehicle shall be calculated as part of the axles and\n\nwheels of the vehicle.\".\n\nMade 31 January 2020\n\n[KKR.PUU.110-1/7/20; PN(PU2)426/LXVIII]\n\n BARU BIAN\n\n Minister of Works"}}],"pack":"my-13"};
  FT["MY-H588"] = {"id":"MY-H588","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-detail.php?act=812&lang=BI","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":97,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2018年财政法","en":"FINANCE ACT 2018","orig":"FINANCE ACT 2018","vi":"Luật về Tài chính năm 2018","th":"พระราชบัญญัติการคลัง ค.ศ. 2018","id":"Undang-Undang Keuangan Tahun 2018","ms":"Akta Kewangan 2018"},"level":"law","category":"02_民商事与经济法","status":"active","docNumber":"ACT812","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2018","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 97 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\02_民商事与经济法\\2018_812_FINANCE ACT 2018.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H588-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"1. This Act may be cited as the Finance Act 2018.\nAmendment of Acts"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"2. The Income Tax Act 1967 [Act 53], the Promotion of Investments\nAct 1986 [ Act 327 ], the Stamp Act 1949 [ Act 378 ], the Real\nProperty Gains Tax Act 1976 [ Act 169 ], the Labuan Business\nActivity Tax Act 1990 [ Act 445 ], the Service Tax Act 2018\n[Act 807 ] and the Sales Tax Act 2018 [ Act 806 ] are amended in\nthe manner specified in Chapters II, III, IV , V , VI, VII and VIII\nrespectively.\nLAWS OF MALAYSIA\nAct 812\nFINANCE ACT 2018\nLaws of Malaysia8\nChapter  II\nAMENDMENTS TO THE INCOME TAX ACT 1967\nCommencement of amendments to the Income Tax Act 1967"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"chapter":{"en":"Chapter II"},"text":{"en":"3. (1) Sections 10, 11, 12, 15, 16, 17, 18, 19, 24, 27, 28, 29\nand 30 and paragraphs 23 (a), (b), (c) and (d) have effect from\nthe year of assessment 2019 and subsequent years of assessment.\n (2) Section 13 has effect for the years of assessment 2019,\n2020 and 2021.\n (3) Section 14 has effect for the years of assessment 2019\nand 2020.\n (4) Paragraph 4 (b) and  sections 5, 6, 6 a, 7, 8, 19 a and\nparagraph 23 (aa) come into operation on the coming into operation\nof this Act.\n (5) Paragraph 4 (a) and sections 9, 20, 21, 22 and 26 come\ninto operation on 1 January 2019.\nAmendment of section 2"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"chapter":{"en":"Chapter II"},"text":{"en":"4. The Income Tax Act 1967, which is referred to as the\n\"principal Act\" in this Chapter, is amended in subsection 2(1)—\n (a) by substituting for the definition of \"Labuan company\"\nthe following definition:\n ‘ \"Labuan company\" means a Labuan entity as\nprovided under subsection 2b(1) of the Labuan Business\nActivity Tax Act 1990;'; and\n (b) by inserting after the definition of \"rent\" the following\ndefinition:\n ‘ \"research and development\" means any systematic,\ninvestigative and experimental study that involves\nnovelty or technical risk carried out in the field of\nscience or technology with the object of acquirin g\nAct 812\nFinance 9\nnew knowledge or using the results of the study for\nthe production or improvement of materials, devices,\nproducts, produce, or processes, but does not include—\n (a) quality control or routine testing of materials,\ndevices or products;\n (b) research in the social sciences or the humanities;\n (c) routine data collection;\n (d) efficiency surveys or management studies;\n (e) market research or sales promotion;\n (f) routine modifications or changes to materials,\ndevices, products, processes or production\nmethods; or\n (g) cosmetic modifications or stylistic changes\nto materials, devices, products, processes or\nproduction methods;'.\nAmendment of section 4a"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"chapter":{"en":"Chapter II"},"text":{"en":"5. Section 4a of the principal Act is amended by substituting\nfor paragraph (ii) the following paragraph:\n \"(ii) amounts paid in consideration of any advice given, or\nassistance or services rendered in connection with the\nmanagement or administration of any scientific, industri al\nor commercial undertaking, venture, project or scheme; or\".\nAmendment of section 12"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6"},"chapter":{"en":"Chapter II"},"text":{"en":"6. Section 12 of the principal Act is amended by inserting after\nsubsection (2) the following subsections:\n \"(3) Notwithstanding subsections (1) and (2), the income\nof a person from a business that is attributable to a place of\nbusiness in Malaysia shall be deemed to be the gross income\nof that person derived from Malaysia from the business.\nLaws of Malaysia10\n (4) For the purpose of subsection (3), a place of business\nincludes—\n (a) a place of management;\n (b) a branch;\n (c) an office;\n (d) a factory;\n (e) a workshop;\n (f) a warehouse;\n (g) a building site, or a construction, an installation or\nan assembly project;\n (h) a farm or plantation; and\n (i) a mine, an oil or gas well, a quarry or any other\nplace of extraction of natural resources,\nand without prejudice to the generality of the foregoing,\na person shall be deemed to have a place of business in\nMalaysia if that person—\n (i) carries on supervisory activities in connection with\na building or work site, or a construction, an\ninstallation or an assembly project; or\n (ii) has another person acting on his behalf who—\n (A) habitually concludes contracts, or habitually\nplays the principal role leading to the\nconclusion of contracts that are routinely\nconcluded without material modification;\n (B) habitually maintains a stock of goods or\nmerchandise in that place of business\nfrom which such person delivers goods\nor merchandise; or\n (C)  regularly fills orders on his behalf.\".\nAct 812\nFinance 11\nAmendment of section 15a\n6a. Section 15 a of the principal Act is amended by substituting\nfor paragraph (b) the following paragraph:\n \"(b) amounts paid in consideration of any advice given, or\nassistance or services rendered in connection with the\nmanagement or administration of any scientific, industri al\nor commercial undertaking, venture, project or scheme;\".\nAmendment of section 34"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7"},"chapter":{"en":"Chapter II"},"text":{"en":"7. Subsection 34(7) of the principal Act is amended by substituting\nfor the words \"scientific research\" the words \"research and\ndevelopment\".\nAmendment of section 34a"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8"},"chapter":{"en":"Chapter II"},"text":{"en":"8. Section 34 a of the principal Act is amended—\n (a) in the shoulder note, by inserting after the word \"research\"\nthe words \"and development\"; and\n (b) in subsections (1), (2) and (5), by inserting after the word\n\"research\" the words \"and development\".\nAmendment of section 39"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9"},"chapter":{"en":"Chapter II"},"text":{"en":"9. Subsection 39(1) of the principal Act is amended—\n (a) by deleting the word \"or\" at the end of paragraph (p);\n (b) by substituting for the full stop at the end of paragraph (q)\nthe words \"; or\"; and\n (c) by inserting after paragraph (q) the following paragraph:\n \" (r) subject to any rules as may be prescribed by the\nMinister, any amount in respect of a payment\nmade by a person, who is a resident, to any\nLabuan company.\".\nLaws of Malaysia12\nAmendment of section 44"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10"},"chapter":{"en":"Chapter II"},"text":{"en":"10. Section 44 of the principal Act is amended by inserting after\nsubsection ( 5e) the following subsection:\n \"( 5f) Notwithstanding subsection (4) or (5), the amount\nascertained under either of those subsections for any relevant\nyear shall only be deductible in accordance with subsection 43(2)\nfor a period of seven consecutive years of assessment and\nthat period commences immediately following the relevant\nyear of assessment and any amount or balance of the amount\nwhich is not deductible at the end of that period shall be\ndisregarded for the purposes of this Act.\".\nSpecial provision relating to sections 43 and 44"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11"},"chapter":{"en":"Chapter II"},"text":{"en":"11. Notwithstanding sections 43 and 44 of the principal Act—\n (a) any amount ascertained under subsection 44(4) or (5) of\nthe principal Act for the year of assessment 2017 and\nthe preceding years of assessment which has not been\ndeducted pursuant to subsection 43(2) of the principal\nAct for the year of assessment 2018; or\n (b) any amount ascertained under subsection 44(4) or (5) of\nthe principal Act for the year of assessment 2018,\nmay be accounted for the purpose of deduction under subsection 43(2)\nof the principal Act for the year of assessment 2019 and subsequent\nyears of assessment until the year of assessment 2025 and any\namount which has not been deducted pursuant to subsection 43(2)\nof the principal Act after the end of the year of assessment 2025\nshall be disregarded for the purposes of the principal Act.\nAmendment of section 44a"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 12"},"chapter":{"en":"Chapter II"},"text":{"en":"12. Section 44a of the principal Act is amended—\n (a) in subsection (1), by inserting after the word \"may\"\nthe words \", for the basis period for three consecutive\nyears of assessment,\";\nAct 812\nFinance 13\n (b) by inserting after subsection (1) the following subsection:\n \"( 1a) For the purpose of subsection (1), the basis period\nfor three consecutive years of assessment commences—\n (a) immediately following the basis period for a year\nof assessment the surrendering company first\ncommences operation, provided that the basis\nperiod consists of a period of twelve months; or\n (b) immediately following the second basis period\nthe surrendering company first commences\noperation (in this paragraph referred to as the\n\"second basis period\"), if the basis period for\na year of assessment the surrendering company\nfirst commences operation is less or more than\ntwelve months and the second basis period\nconsists of a period of twelve months.\";\n (c) in subsection (10), by inserting after paragraph (a) the\nfollowing paragraph:\n \" (aa) has unutilized investment tax allowance or\nadjusted loss from a pioneer business under\nthe Promotion of Investments Act 1986;\"; and\n (d) in subsection (12)—\n (i) in the definition of \"ordinary shares\", by deleting\nthe word \"nominal\"; and\n (ii) in the definition of \"residual profits\", by deleting\nthe word \"nominal\".\nSpecial provision relating to section 44a"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 13"},"chapter":{"en":"Chapter II"},"text":{"en":"13. Notwithstanding subsection 44a(1) of the principal Act as\namended in this Act, a surrendering company may surrender its\nadjusted loss for the basis period for a year of assessment in\naccordance with that subsection for the basis period of—\n (a) the year of assessment 2019, in relation to a surrendering\ncompany which first commences its operation in the\nyear of assessment 2015;\nLaws of Malaysia14\n (b) the years of assessment 2019 and 2020, in relation to a\nsurrendering company which first commences its operation\nin the year of assessment 2016; and\n (c) the years of assessment 2019, 2020 and 2021, in relation\nto a surrendering company which first commences its\noperation in the year of assessment 2017.\nAmendment of section 46"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A14","no":14,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 14"},"chapter":{"en":"Chapter II"},"text":{"en":"14. Paragraph 46(1) (k) of the principal Act is amended by\nsubstituting for the word \"six\" wherever appearing the word\n\"eight\".\nAmendment of section 49"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A15","no":15,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 15"},"chapter":{"en":"Chapter II"},"text":{"en":"15. Section 49 of the principal Act is amended—\n (a) by substituting for subsection (1) the following subsection:\n \"(1) Subject to this section, in the case of an\nindividual resident for the basis year for a year of\nassessment, there shall be allowed for that year of\nassessment a deduction—\n (a) not exceeding three thousand ringgit, in respect\nof premium paid by that individual for any\ninsurance;\n (b) not exceeding four thousand ringgit, in respect\nof contribution to approved scheme (other than\na private retirement scheme) made or suffered\nby that individual who is an employee or\na self-employed person within the meaning\nof the Employees Provident Fund Act 1991\n[Act 452 ]; or\n (c) not exceeding four thousand ringgit, in respect\nof any amount made or suffered by that\nindividual on any contribution under any written\nlaw relating to widow, widower and orphan's\npension or under any approved scheme within\nthe meaning of any such law.\"; and\nAct 812\nFinance 15\n (b) by substituting for subsection (1a) the following subsection:\n \"(1 a) For the purpose of subsection (1)—\n (a) the total amount of deduction under subsection (1)\nshall not exceed seven thousand ringgit;\n (b) where subsection 50(2) or 50(3) applies, the\namount of deduction to be allowed shall be in\naccordance with paragraphs (1) (a), (b) and (c)\nand the total deduction under subsection 50(2)\nor (3) shall not exceed seven thousand ringgit;\n (c) in the case of an individual who is a pensionable\nofficer within the meaning of section 2 of\nthe Pensions Act 1980 [ Act 227 ] and no\ndeduction is made under paragraph (1) (b)\nor (c) to that individual, the amount of deduction\nunder paragraph (1) (a) shall not exceed seven\nthousand ringgit.\".\nAmendment of section 60"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A16","no":16,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 16"},"chapter":{"en":"Chapter II"},"text":{"en":"16. Section 60 of the principal Act is amended—\n (a) in subsection (2)—\n (i) by substituting for paragraph (b) the following\nparagraph:\n \" (b) where an insurer carries on re-insurance\nbusiness, the re-insurance business and\nthe general business (excluding the\nre-insurance business) shall be treated\nas separate general businesses;\"; and\n (ii) in paragraph (c), by substituting for the proviso\nthe following proviso:\n \"Provided that where the insurer also\ncarries on life re-insurance business, the life\nre-insurance business shall be a separate source\nfrom life business and shall be treated as a\ngeneral business;\";\nLaws of Malaysia16\n (b) in subsection (5a), by deleting the word \"inward\" wherever\nappearing;\n (c) by deleting subsection ( 5b);\n (d) in subsection (6a), by deleting the word \"inward\" wherever\nappearing;\n (e) by deleting subsection ( 6b);\n (f) in subsection (7), by substituting for the words \", ( 6a)\nor ( 6b)\" the words \"or ( 6a)\"; and\n (g) in subsection (11)—\n (i) by substituting for the words \", sections 60a\nand 60b\" the words \"and section 60a\"; and\n (ii) by deleting the definitions of \"inward\nre-insurance\", \"inward re-insurance contract\",\n\"offshore insurance\" and \"offshore insurance\npolicies\".\nAmendment of section 60a"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A17","no":17,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 17"},"chapter":{"en":"Chapter II"},"text":{"en":"17. Section 60a of the principal Act is amended—\n (a) in the shoulder note, by substituting for the words\n\"Inward re-insurance\" the word \"Re-insurance\";\n (b) by deleting the word \"inward\" wherever appearing;\n (c) in subsection (2), by substituting for the words\n\"5 per cent\" the words \"8 per cent\"; and\n (d) by inserting after subsection (2) the following subsection:\n \"(3) This section shall apply to an insurer who\nhas an adequate number of full time employees and\nhas incurred an adequate amount of annual operating\nexpenditure in Malaysia as prescribed by the Minister.\".\nAct 812\nFinance 17\nAmendment of section 60aa"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A18","no":18,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 18"},"chapter":{"en":"Chapter II"},"text":{"en":"18. Section 60aa of the principal Act is amended—\n (a) by substituting for subsection (1) the following subsection:\n \"(1) This section shall apply—\n (a) for ascertaining the adjusted income for\nthe basis period for a year of assessment from\nthe takaful business of a takaful operator; and\n (b) to a takaful operator who has an adequate number\nof full time employees and has incurred an\nadequate amount of annual operating expenditure\nin Malaysia as prescribed by the Minister.\";\n (b) in subsection (2)—\n (i) by substituting for paragraph (b) the following\nparagraph:\n \" (b) where the takaful operator carries on\na re-takaful business, the re-takaful\nbusiness and the general takaful\nbusiness (excluding the re-takaful\nbusiness) shall be treated as separate\ngeneral takaful businesses;\";\n (ii) in paragraph (c), by substituting for the proviso\nthe following proviso:\n \"Provided that where the takaful operator\nalso carries on family re-takaful business,\nthe family re-takaful business shall be a separate\nsource from the family business and shall be\ntreated as a general takaful business;\"; and\n (iii) by substituting for paragraph (e) the following\nparagraph:\n \" (e) where a takaful operator carries on\nre-takaful business which includes\nfamily re-takaful business and general\ntakaful business (excluding those\nbusinesses), the income of the fund\nLaws of Malaysia18\nestablished in respect of each of the\nbusinesses (in this section referred to\nas \"re-takaful fund\", \"family re-takaful\nfund\" and \"general fund\" respectively)\nshall be treated as a separate source\nof income from the income of the\nshareholders' fund in respect of those\nbusinesses.\";\n (c) by substituting for subsection (6) the following subsection:\n \"(6) The adjusted income of the re-takaful fund or\nfamily re-takaful fund for the basis period for a year of\nassessment in respect of re-takaful business, or family\nre-takaful business respectively of a takaful operator\nresident for the basis year for that year of assessment\nshall consist of an amount arrived at by applying\nsubsection (5) and references in that subsection to—\n (a) \"general takaful certificate\" shall be construed as\nreferences to \"re-takaful contract\" or \"takaful\ncertificate in relation to its family re-takaful\nbusiness\", as the case may be;\n (b) \"general takaful business\" shall be construed as\nreferences to \"re-takaful business\" or \"family\nre-takaful business\", as the case may be; and\n (c) \"reserve fund for unexpired risks\" and\n\"takaful operator\" shall, in the case of\nfamily re-takaful business, be construed as\nreferences to \"actuarial valuation reserve\" and\n\"family takaful operator\" respectively:\n Provided that in the case of re-takaful business, no\ndeduction shall be allowed on any share of profits\ndistributed or credited to the takaful participant or\nshareholders' fund for that period out of any of the\ntakaful operator's fund, as the case may be.\";\n (d) by substituting for subsection (8) the following subsection:\n \"(8) The adjusted income of the re-takaful fund,\nor family re-takaful fund for the basis period for a\nyear of assessment in respect of re-takaful business\nor family re-takaful business respectively of a takaful\noperator not resident for the basis year for that year\nAct 812\nFinance 19\nof assessment shall, where that business is wholly or\npartly carried on in Malaysia, consist of an amount\narrived at by applying subsection (7) and references\nin that subsection to—\n (a) \"Malaysian general takaful certificate\" shall be\nconstrued as references to \"re-takaful contract\"\nor \"Malaysian takaful certificate in relation to its\nfamily re-takaful business\", as the case may be;\n (b) \"general takaful business\" shall be construed as\nreferences to \"re-takaful business\" or \"family\nre-takaful business\", as the case may be; and\n (c) \"reserve fund for unexpired risks\" and \"takaful\noperator\" shall, in the case of family re-takaful\nbusiness, be construed as references to \"actuarial\nvaluation reserve\" and \"family takaful operator\"\nrespectively:\n Provided that in the case of re-takaful business, no\ndeduction shall be allowed on any share of profits\ndistributed or credited to the takaful participant or\nshareholders' fund for that period out of any of the\ntakaful operator's re-takaful fund, as the case may be.\";\n (e) in subparagraph (9) (a)(iii), by deleting the words \"inward\"\nand \"offshore fund\";\n (f) in subparagraph (10)(a)(iii), by deleting the words \"inward\"\nand \"offshore fund\";\n (g) in subsection (20), by deleting the words \"inward\" and\n\"or offshore takaful business\" wherever appearing;\n (h) in subsection (21), by deleting the words \"inward\" and\n\"or offshore takaful business\";\n (i) in subsection (22)—\n (i) by deleting the words \"inward\" and \"or offshore\ntakaful business\" wherever appearing; and\n (ii) by substituting for the word \"five\" the word\n\"eight\"; and\nLaws of Malaysia20\n (j) in subsection (23), by deleting the definitions of\n\"inward re-takaful\", \"inward re-takaful contract\" and\n\"offshore takaful\".\nDeletion of section 60b"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A19","no":19,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 19"},"chapter":{"en":"Chapter II"},"text":{"en":"19. The principal Act is amended by deleting section 60b.\nAmendment of section 109 b\n19a. Section 109 b of the principal Act is amended by substituting\nfor paragraph (b) the following paragraph:\n \" (b) for any advice given, or assistance or services rendered\nin connection with the management or administration\nof any scientific, industrial or commercial undertaking,\nventure, project or scheme;\".\nAmendment of section 140 a"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A20","no":20,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 20"},"chapter":{"en":"Chapter II"},"text":{"en":"20. Section 140a of the principal Act is amended—\n (a) in paragraph (5) (c), by inserting after the word \"person\"\nthe words \"(in this section referred to as \"third person\")\";\nand\n (b) by inserting after subsection (5) the following subsection:\n \"( 5a) Without prejudice to the generality of\nsection 139, for the purpose of subsection (5), \"control\"\nrefers to persons one of whom owns shares of the other\nperson, or a third person who owns shares of both\npersons, where the percentage of the share capital held\nin either situation is twenty per cent or more and—\n (a) the business operations of that person depends\non the proprietary rights, such as patents,\nnon-patented technological know-how,\ntrademarks, or copyrights, provided by the\nother person or a third person;\nAct 812\nFinance 21\n (b) the business activities, such as purchases, sales,\nreceipt of services, provision of services, of\nthat person are specified by the other person,\nand the prices and other conditions relating\nto the supply are influenced by such other\nperson or a third person; or\n (c) where one or more of the directors or members of\nthe board of directors of a person are appointed\nby the other person or a third person.\".\nNew section 140 c"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A21","no":21,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 21"},"chapter":{"en":"Chapter II"},"text":{"en":"21. The principal Act is amended by inserting after section 140b\nthe following section:\n\"Restriction on deductibility of interest\n140 c. (1) This section shall apply without prejudice to\nsection 140 or 140a and subject to any rules made under\nthis Act.\n (2) In ascertaining the adjusted income of a person from\neach of his sources consisting of a business for the basis\nperiod for a year of assessment, no deduction from the gross\nincome from that source for that period shall be allowed\nin respect of any interest expense in connection with or on\nany financial assistance in a controlled transaction granted\ndirectly or indirectly to that person which is in excess of\nthe maximum amount of interest as determined under any\nrules made under this Act.\n (3) In this section—\n \"control\" has the meaning assigned to it in subsection 140a(5a);\n \"controlled transaction\" shall be construed as a financial\nassistance—\n (a) between  persons one of whom has control over the\nother; or\n (b ) between persons both of whom are controlled by\nsome other person (in this section referred to as\n\"third person\");\nLaws of Malaysia22\n \"financial assistance\" includes loan, interest bearing trade\ncredit, advances, debt or the provision of any security or\nguarantee;\n \"interest expense\" means—\n (a) interest on all forms of debt; or\n (b) payments economically equivalent to interest\n(excluding expenses incurred in connection with\nthe raising of finance).\".\nAmendment of section 154"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A22","no":22,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 22"},"chapter":{"en":"Chapter II"},"text":{"en":"22. Paragraph 154(1) (ed)  of the principal Act is amended\nby substituting for the words \"section 140 a\" the words\n\"sections 140 a and 140c\".\nAmendment of Schedule 1"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A23","no":23,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 23"},"chapter":{"en":"Chapter II"},"text":{"en":"23. Schedule 1 to the principal Act is amended—\n (a) in Part I—\n (i) in paragraph 2a, in the column Rate of income\ntax in item 1, by substituting for the words\n\"18 per cent\" the words \"17 per cent\";\n (ii) in paragraph 2d, in the column Rate of income\ntax in item 1, by substituting for the words\n\"18 per cent\" the words \"17 per cent\";\n (iii) by substituting for paragraph 3 the following\nparagraph:\n\"3. Income tax shall be charged for a year of assessment\non the chargeable income of an insurer from a\nre-insurance business at the rate of 8 per cent on every\nringgit of the chargeable income. \"; and\n (iv) by substituting for paragraph 4 the following\nparagraph:\n\"4. Income tax shall be charged for a year of assessment\non the chargeable income of a takaful operator from a\nre-takaful business at the rate of 8 per cent on every\nringgit of the chargeable income.\";\nAct 812\nFinance 23\n (aa) in Part V , by substituting for paragraph (ii) the following\nparagraph:\n \"(ii) amounts paid in consideration of any advice given,\nor assistance or services rendered in connection\nwith the management or administration of any\nscientific, industrial or commercial undertaking,\nventure, project or scheme; or\";\n (b) by substituting for Part VIII the following Part:\n\"part VIII\nNotwithstanding Part I and Part II, income tax shall be charged\non the chargeable income of a life fund, other than income arising\nfrom life re-insurance business of a resident or non-resident\ninsurer at the rate of .. .. .. 8 per cent.\";\n (c) in Part IX, by inserting after the words \"10 per cent\"\nthe words \"for the years of assessment 2019 and 2020\nand 24 per cent for the subsequent years of assessment\";\nand\n (d) by substituting for Part XII the following Part:\n\"part XII\nNotwithstanding Part I and Part II, income tax shall be\ncharged on the chargeable income of a family fund referred\nto in section 60aa, other than income arising from a family\nre-takaful business of a resident or non-resident operator at the\nrate of .. .. .. .. .. .. ..8 per cent.\".\nAmendment of Schedule 3"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A24","no":24,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 24"},"chapter":{"en":"Chapter II"},"text":{"en":"24. Schedule 3 to the principal Act is amended—\n (a) in paragraph 37b—\n (i) in subparagraph (a), by inserting after the word\n\"research\" the words \"and development\";\nLaws of Malaysia24\n (ii) in subparagraph (e), by inserting before the word\n\"undertaken\" the words \"and development\";\n (iii) by inserting after the words \"such research\"\nwherever appearing the words \"and development\";\nand\n (iv) by inserting after the words \"in the case of\nresearch\" the words \"and development\"; and\n (b) in paragraph 37d, by inserting after the word \"research\"\nthe words \"and development\".\n (c) ( Deleted )\n (d) ( Deleted )"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A25","no":25,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 25"},"chapter":{"en":"Chapter II"},"text":{"en":"25. (Deleted )\nAmendment of Schedule 6"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A26","no":26,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 26"},"chapter":{"en":"Chapter II"},"text":{"en":"26. Paragraph 35a of Schedule 6 to the principal Act is amended\nby substituting for the proviso the following proviso:\n \"Provided that the exemption shall not apply to the interest paid or\ncredited to a unit trust that is a wholesale fund which is a money market\nfund.\".\nAmendment of Schedule 7a"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A27","no":27,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 27"},"chapter":{"en":"Chapter II"},"text":{"en":"27. Schedule 7a to the principal Act is amended—\n (a) in paragraph 4, by deleting the words \"until the person\nhas received the whole of the allowance or allowances\nto which it is so entitled\"; and\n (b) by inserting after paragraph 4a the following paragraph:\n\"4b. Notwithstanding paragraph 4, so much of the allowance\nor allowances as cannot be given as ascertained under that\nparagraph at the end of the fifteen consecutive years of assessment\nreferred to in paragraph 2 (in this paragraph referred to as\n\"the first mentioned year of assessment\"), shall only be given to\nthat person in accordance with paragraph 4 for a period of seven\nAct 812\nFinance 25\nconsecutive years of assessment (in this paragraph referred to as\n\"that period\") and that period commences immediately after the\nend of the first mentioned year of assessment, and any amount\nof that allowance or that allowances at the end of that period\nwhich cannot be given to that person, by reason of insufficiency\nor absence of statutory income from a business of his for that\nperiod, shall be disregarded for the purpose of this Schedule.\".\nSpecial provision relating to paragraph 4b of Schedule 7a"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A28","no":28,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 28"},"chapter":{"en":"Chapter II"},"text":{"en":"28. Notwithstanding paragraph 4 of Schedule 7a to the principal\nAct and paragraph 4b of that Schedule as introduced by section 27\nof this Act, so much of that allowance as cannot be given under\nparagraph 4 of that Schedule before the coming into operation\nof section 27 of this Act for the year of assessment 2018 and\nthat amount relates to allowance ascertained at the end of the\nfifteen consecutive years of assessment referred to in paragraph 2\nof that Schedule or allowance ascertained for the year of\nassessment 2018 as provided for under paragraph 2b—\n (a) shall only be given to that person in accordance with\nparagraph 4 of Schedule 7a to the principal Act, as if\nthe principal Act has not been amended, for a period\nof seven consecutive years of assessment and that\nperiod commences immediately following the year of\nassessment 2018; and\n (b) any amount of that allowance or that aggregate amount\nat the end of that period which has not been given to\nthat person, by reason of insufficiency or absence of\nstatutory income from a business of his for that period,\nshall be disregarded for the purpose of Schedule 7a of\nthe principal Act.\nAmendment of Schedule 7b"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A29","no":29,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 29"},"chapter":{"en":"Chapter II"},"text":{"en":"29. Schedule 7b to the principal Act is amended—\n (a) in paragraph 5, by deleting the words \"until the company\nhas received the whole of the allowance or allowances\nto which it is so entitled\"; and\nLaws of Malaysia26\n (b) by inserting after paragraph 5 the following paragraph:\n\"5a. Notwithstanding paragraph 5, so much of the allowance\nor allowances as cannot be given as ascertained under that\nparagraph for the year of assessment that relates to the basis\nperiod where the five-year period specified in paragraph 3 ends\n(in this paragraph referred to as \"the first mentioned year of\nassessment\"), shall only be given to that person in accordance\nwith paragraph 5 for a period of seven consecutive years of\nassessment (in this paragraph referred to as \"that period\") and\nthat period commences immediately after the end of the first\nmentioned year of assessment, and any amount of that allowance\nor those allowances at the end of that period which cannot be\ngiven to that person, by reason of insufficiency or absence of\nstatutory income from a business of his for that period, shall be\ndisregarded for the purpose of this Schedule.\".\nSpecial provision relating to paragraph 5a of Schedule 7b"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A30","no":30,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 30"},"chapter":{"en":"Chapter II"},"text":{"en":"30. Notwithstanding paragraph 5 of Schedule 7b to the principal\nAct and paragraph 5a of that Schedule as introduced by section 29\nof this Act, any allowance or allowances which cannot be given\nunder paragraph 5 of Schedule 7b to the principal Act before\nthe coming into operation of section 29 of this Act for the year\nof assessment 2018 and that amount relates to the allowance or\nallowances ascertained under paragraph 5 of Schedule 7b to the\nprincipal Act before the coming into operation of section 29 of\nthis Act for the year of assessment that relates to the basis period\nwhere the five-year period specified in paragraph 3 ends—\n (a) shall only be given to that person in accordance with\nparagraph 5 of Schedule 7b to the principal Act, as if\nthe principal Act has not been amended, for a period\nof seven consecutive years of assessment and that\nperiod commences immediately following the year of\nassessment 2018; and\n (b) any amount of that allowance or that aggregate amount\nat the end of that period which has not been given\nto that person, by reason of insufficiency or absence\nof statutory income from a business of his for those\nperiod, shall be disregarded for the purpose of Schedule 7b\nof the principal Act.\nAct 812\nFinance 27\nchapter  III\nAMENDMENTS TO THE PROMOTION OF INVESTMENTS ACT 1986\nCommencement of amendments to the Promotion of Investments\nAct 1986"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A31","no":31,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 31"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"31. (1) Section 32 comes into operation on the coming into\noperation of this Act.\n (2) Sections 36, 37 and 62 have effect from the year of\nassessment 2019 and subsequent years of assessment.\n (3) Sections 33, 34 and 35 come into operation on 1 January 2019.\nAmendment of section 2"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A32","no":32,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 32"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"32. Section 2 of the Promotion of Investments Act 1986\nwhich is referred to as the \"principal Act\" in this Chapter, is\namended by substituting for the definition of \"research and\ndevelopment\" the following definition:\n ‘ \"research and development\" means any systematic,\ninvestigative and experimental study that involves novelty or\ntechnical risk carried out in the field of science or technology\nwith the object of acquiring new knowledge or using the results\nof the study for the production or improvement of materials,\ndevices, products, produce, or processes, but does not include—\n (a) quality control or routine testing of materials, devices\nor products;\n (b) research in the social sciences or the humanities;\n (c) routine data collections;\n (d) efficiency surveys or management studies;\n (e) market research or sales promotion;\n (f) routine modifications or changes to materials, devices,\nproducts, processes or production methods; or\n (g) cosmetic modifications or stylistic changes to materials,\ndevices, products, processes or production methods.\".\nLaws of Malaysia28\nAmendment of section 6"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A33","no":33,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 33"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"33. Subsection 6( 1ac) of the principal Act is amended—\n (a) by substituting for the full stop at end of the subsection\na colon; and\n (b) by inserting the following proviso:\n \"Provided that the contract research and development\ncompany at the time of application has an adequate\nnumber of full time employees and incurred adequate\namount of annual operating expenditure in Malaysia\nfor an activity relating to research and development.\".\nSpecial provision relating to section 6"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A34","no":34,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 34"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"34. Notwithstanding the proviso of subsection 6( 1ac) of the\nprincipal Act as introduced by section 33 of this Act—\n (a) where a contract research and development company has\nbeen granted a pioneer status on or before 16 October 2017,\nthe proviso to subsection 6( 1ac) shall not apply to that\ncompany until 30 June 2021; and\n (b) where a contract research and development company has\nbeen granted a pioneer status after 16 October 2017,\nthe proviso to subsection 6( 1ac) shall not apply to that\ncompany until 31 December 2018.\nAmendment of section 21e"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A35","no":35,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 35"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"35. Section 21e of the principal Act is amended by inserting\nafter subsection (2) the following subsections:\n \"( 2a) For the avoidance of doubt, the income of a pioneer\ncompany referred to in subsection (2) shall not include any\nincome from royalty and other income derived from an\nintellectual property right if it is receivable as consideration\nfor the commercial exploitation of that right.\nAct 812\nFinance 29\n ( 2b) Any income derived from intellectual property right\nreferred to in subsection ( 2a) is subject to tax under the Income\nTax Act 1967.\n ( 2c) For the purpose of this section, \"intellectual property\nright\" means a right arising from any patent, utility innovation\nand discovery, copyright, trade mark and service mark, industrial\ndesign, layout-design of integrated circuit, secret processes or\nformulae and know-how, geographical indication and the grant\nof protection of a plant variety, and other like rights, whether\nor not registered or registrable.\".\nAmendment of section 25"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A36","no":36,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 36"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"36. Section 25 of the principal Act is amended—\n (a) by deleting subsection (3);\n (b) in subsection (4), by deleting the proviso; and\n (c) by inserting after subsection (4) the following subsection:\n \"(5) Notwithstanding subsection (4), the deduction\nwhich has not been so made (or so much thereof\nas has not been so made) for a year of assessment\nunder that subsection, shall only be made to that\ncompany in accordance with that subsection for a\nperiod of seven consecutive years of assessment and\nthat period commences immediately following the\nyear of assessment that relates to the basis period in\nwhich the day the post pioneer business falls, and any\namount of deduction at the end of that period which\nhas not been so made to that company, by reason of\ninsufficiency or absence of statutory income for that\nperiod, shall be disregarded for the purpose of this\nsection.\".\nSpecial provision relating to section 25"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A37","no":37,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 37"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"37. Notwithstanding subsection 25(4) of the principal Act as\namended by section 36 of this Act and subsection 25(5) of the\nprincipal Act as introduced by section 36 of this Act, any amount\nLaws of Malaysia30\nof deduction which cannot be made under subsection 25(4) of\nthe principal Act for the year of assessment 2018 and preceding\nyears of assessment—\n (a) shall only be made to that company in accordance with\nsubsection 25(4) of the principal Act for a period\nof seven consecutive years of assessment and that\nperiod commences immediately following the year of\nassessment 2018; and\n (b) any amount of deduction at the end of that period which\nhas not been so made to that company, by reason of\ninsufficiency or absence of statutory income from its\nbusiness for that period, shall be disregarded for the\npurposes of the principal Act."}},{"id":"MY-H588-A38","no":38,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 38"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"38. (Deleted )"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A39","no":39,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 39"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"39. (Deleted )"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A40","no":40,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 40"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"40. (Deleted )"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A41","no":41,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 41"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"41. (Deleted )"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A42","no":42,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 42"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"42. (Deleted )"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A43","no":43,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 43"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"43. (Deleted )"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A44","no":44,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 44"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"44. (Deleted )"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A45","no":45,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 45"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"45. (Deleted )"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A46","no":46,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 46"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"46. (Deleted )"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A47","no":47,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 47"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"47. (Deleted )"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A48","no":48,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 48"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"48. (Deleted )"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A49","no":49,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 49"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"49. (Deleted )"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A50","no":50,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 50"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"50. (Deleted )"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A51","no":51,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 51"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"51. (Deleted )"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A52","no":52,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 52"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"52. (Deleted )\nAct 812\nFinance 31"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A53","no":53,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 53"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"53. (Deleted )"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A54","no":54,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 54"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"54. (Deleted )"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A55","no":55,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 55"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"55. (Deleted )"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A56","no":56,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 56"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"56. (Deleted )"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A57","no":57,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 57"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"57. (Deleted )"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A58","no":58,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 58"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"58. (Deleted )"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A59","no":59,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 59"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"59. (Deleted )"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A60","no":60,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 60"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"60. (Deleted )"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A61","no":61,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 61"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"61. ( Deleted )\nAmendment of section 30a"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A62","no":62,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 62"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter III"},"text":{"en":"62. Subsection 30 a(1) of the principal Act is amended by\nsubstituting for the word \"two\" the word \"five\".\nchapter  IV\nAMENDMENTS TO THE STAMP ACT 1949\nCommencement of amendments to the Stamp Act 1949"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A63","no":63,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 63"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter IV"},"text":{"en":"63. (1) Sections 64, 65, 66, 67 and paragraphs 68 (a), (b), (c)\nand (e) commence on the coming into operation of this Act.\n (2) Paragraph 68 (d) comes into operation on 1 January 2019.\nAmendment of section 2"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A64","no":64,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 64"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter IV"},"text":{"en":"64. The Stamp Act 1949, which is referred to as the \"principal Act\"\nin this Chapter, is amended in section 2—\n (a) by substituting for the definition of \"banker\" the following\ndefinition:\n  ‘ \"banker\" means—\n (a) any person licensed under the Financial Services\nAct 2013 [ Act 758 ] to carry on a banking\nbusiness in Malaysia;\nLaws of Malaysia32\n (b) any person licensed under the Islamic Financial\nServices Act 2013 [ Act 759 ] to carry on an\nIslamic banking business in Malaysia; or\n (c) a development financial institution prescribed\nunder the Development Financial Institutions\nAct 2002 [ Act 618 ];'; and\n (b) by substituting for the definition of \"small and medium\nenterprise\" the following definition:\n  ‘ \"small and medium enterprise\" means—\n (a) in relation to the manufacturing activities, an\nenterprise with sales turnover not exceeding\nfifty million ringgit or full-time employees not\nexceeding two hundred people; or\n (b) in relation to the services, and other sectors, an\nenterprise with sales turnover not exceeding\ntwenty million ringgit or full-time employees\nnot exceeding seventy-five people;'.\nAmendment of section 9"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A65","no":65,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 65"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter IV"},"text":{"en":"65. Section 9 of the principal Act is amended—\n (a) by subsituting for subsection (1) the following subsection:\n \"(1) The Collector, may by notification in the\nGazette , authorize any person including any banker,\ndealer or insurer, to compound for the payment of duty\non unstamped instrument subject to the condition that\nthe instrument be drawn or drawn up and issued on a\nform to be supplied or adopted by the said person.\";\nand\n (b) in subsection (6), by substituting for the words\n\"as mentioned under paragraph 1 (a), (b) or (c)\" the\nwords \"under subsection (1)\".\nAct 812\nFinance 33\nAmendment of section 15"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A66","no":66,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 66"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter IV"},"text":{"en":"66. Section 15 of the principal Act is amended—\n (a) by substituting for the words \"nominal share capital\"\nwherever appearing the words \"issued share capital\";\n (b) by deleting subsection (2);\n (c) in subsection (5)—\n (i) in paragraph (b), by substituting for the words\n\"two years\" the words \"three years\"; and\n (ii) in paragraph (c), by substituting for the words\n\"two years\" the words \"three years\"; and\n (d) by inserting after subsection (6) the following subsection:\n \"( 6a) Where any claim for exemption from duty\nunder this section has been allowed and any of\nthe circumstances specified under subsection (5) occurs,\neach company which was a party to the instrument\nshall notify the Collector of the circumstances of\nthe occurrence within thirty days from the date of\nthe occurrence.\".\nAmendment of section 15a"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A67","no":67,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 67"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter IV"},"text":{"en":"67. Section 15a of the principal Act is amended—\n (a) by substituting for subsection (2) the following subsection:\n \"(2) This section applies to any instrument with\nrespect to which it is shown to the satisfaction of\nthe Collector—\n (a) that the effect is to transfer a beneficial interest\nin property from one company with limited\nliability to another such company, and that\nthe companies are associated where one is the\nbeneficial owner of not less than ninety per\ncent of the issued share capital of the other,\nLaws of Malaysia34\nor that a third company with limited liability\nis the beneficial owner of not less than ninety\nper centum of the issued share capital of each\nof the aforesaid companies;\n (b) that the transfer of the property of the associated\ncompanies is to achieve greater efficiency in\noperation; and\n (c ) that the company referred to as the transferee\ncompany under this section is incorporated in\nMalaysia.\";\n (b) in subsection (4)—\n (i) in paragraph (c)—\n (A) by inserting after the word \"company\"\nthe words \"within the period of three\nyears from the date of the conveyance\nor transfer,\"; and\n (B) by substituting for the comma at the end\nof paragraph (c) the words \"; or\"; and\n (ii) by inserting after paragraph (c) the following\nparagraph:\n \" (d) the transferee company disposes of\nthe property that it has acquired within\nthree years from the date of the conveyance\nor transfer of the property,\"; and\n (c) by inserting after subsection (4) the following subsections:\n \"(5) Where any claim for exemption from duty\nunder this section has been allowed, it is subsequently\nfound that any declaration or other evidence furnished\nin support of the claim is untrue, the exemption\nfrom duty shall be revoked and duty shall be\nchargeable, together with interest thereon at the rate of\nsix per centum per annum, from the date on which\nthe duty which the conveyance or transfer ought to\nbe stamped with the proper amount of duty.\nAct 812\nFinance 35\n (6) Where any claim for exemption from duty\nunder this section has been allowed and any of the\ncircumstances specified under subsection (4) occurs,\neach company which was a party to the instrument shall\nnotify the Collector in writing of the circumstances\nof the occurrence within thirty days from the date of\nthe occurrence.\n (7) Where a claim is made for exemption under\nthis section, the Collector may require the delivery\nto him of a statutory declaration in such form as he\nmay direct made by an advocate and solicitor, or, in\nthe case of Sabah and Sarawak, an advocate, of the\nHigh Court, and of such further evidence, if any, as\nhe deems necessary.\".\nAmendment of First Schedule"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A68","no":68,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 68"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter IV"},"text":{"en":"68. The First Schedule to the principal Act is amended—\n (a) by deleting item 10;\n (b) in item 22—\n (i) by substituting for subitem (1) the following\nsubitem:\n\"(1) Being the only or principal\nor primary security for any\nannuity (except upon the\noriginal creation thereof\nby way of sale or security,\nand except a superannuation\nannuity), or for any sum or\nsums of money at stated\nperiods, not being interest for\nany sum secured by a duly\nstamped instrument, nor rent\nreserved by a lease or tack—\n (a) for a definite and certain\nperiod so that the\ntotal amount to be\nultimately payable can\nbe ascertained\nThe same a d\nvalorem duty as a\ncharge or mortgage\nfor such total\namount.\nLaws of Malaysia36\n (b) for the term of life or\nany other indefinite\nperiod—\nfor every RM100\nand also for any\nfractional part of\nRM100 of the\nannuity or sum\nperiodically payable\nRM1.00\n\"; and\n (ii) in subitem (6), by inserting after the words\n\"in accordance with the\" the words \"conventional\nhire purchase and\";\n (c) by inserting after item 29 the following item:\n \"29 a CONSTITUTION OF A\nCOMPANY\nRM200.00\";\n (d) in subitem 32 (a), in the column Proper Stamp Duty —\n (i) in item (iii), by substituting for the words\n\"RM500,000.\" the words \"RM500,000 but not\nexceeding RM1,000,000;\"; and\n (ii) by inserting after item (iii) the following item:\n \"(iv) RM4.00 on any amount in excess of\nRM1,000,000.\"; and\n (e) by deleting item 53.\nchapter  V\nAMENDMENTS TO THE REAL PROPERTY GAINS TAX ACT 1976\nCommencement of amendments to the Real Property Gains\nTax Act 1976"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A69","no":69,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 69"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter V"},"text":{"en":"69. This Chapter comes into operation on 1 January 2019.\nAct 812\nFinance 37\nAmendment of Schedule 2\n69a. The Real Property Gains Tax Act 1976 which is referred\nto as the \"principal Act\" in this Chapter, is amended in\nSchedule 2—\n (a) by inserting after paragraph 2 the following paragraph:\n\"2a For the purposes of this Schedule, where a disposal\nis subject to tax under Part I of Schedule 5, references\nto 1 January 1970 shall be construed as references to\n1 January 2000.\"; and\n (b) in subparagraph 12(2) (c), by deleting the words \"where\nthe gift is made within five years after the date of\nacquisition by the donor,\".\nAmendment of Schedule 3\n69b. The principal Act is amended in Schedule 3 in subparagraph 13(2)\nby substituting for the words \"1 January 1970\" wherever appearing\nthe words \"1 January 2000\".\nAmendment of Schedule 5"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A70","no":70,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 70"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter V"},"text":{"en":"70. The Principal Act is amended in Schedule 5—\n (a) in Part I, in the column \"Rate of tax\" in item 4,\nby substituting for the word \"Nil\" the words \"5 per cent\";\n (b) in Part II, in the column \"Rate of tax\" in item 4,\nby substituting for the words \"5 per cent\" the words\n\"10 per cent\"; and\n (c) in Part III, in the column \"Rate of tax\" in item 2,\nby substituting for the words \"5 per cent\" dengan\n\"10 per cent\".\nLaws of Malaysia38\nchapter  VI\nAMENDMENTS TO THE LABUAN BUSINESS ACTIVITY\nTAX ACT 1990\nCommencement of amendments to the Labuan Business Activity\nTax Act 1990"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A71","no":71,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 71"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter VI"},"text":{"en":"71. This Chapter comes into operation on 1 January 2019.\nAmendment of section 2"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A72","no":72,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 72"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter VI"},"text":{"en":"72. The Labuan Business Activity Tax Act 1990, which is\nreferred to as the \"principal Act\" in this Chapter, is amended in\nsubsection 2(1)—\n (a) by substituting for the definition of \"Labuan business\nactivity\" the following definition:\n ‘ \"Labuan business activity\" means a Labuan trading\nor a Labuan non-trading activity carried on in, from\nor through Labuan, excluding any activity which is\nan offence under any written law;'; and\n (b) by deleting the definition of \"Labuan entity\".\nAmendment of section 2a"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A73","no":73,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 73"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter VI"},"text":{"en":"73. Section 2a of the principal Act is amended by deleting\nsubsection (2).\nAmendment of section 2b"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A74","no":74,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 74"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter VI"},"text":{"en":"74. Section 2b of the principal Act is amended by substituting\nfor subsection (1) the following subsection:\n \"(1) The Labuan entities—\n (a) shall be as specified in the Schedule; and\nAct 812\nFinance 39\n (b) shall, for the purpose of the Labuan business activity,\nhave—\n (i) an adequate number of full time employees in\nLabuan; and\n (ii) an adequate amount of annual operating expenditure\nin Labuan,\n  as prescribed by the Minister by regulations made under\nthis Act.\".\nAmendment of section 4"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A75","no":75,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 75"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter VI"},"text":{"en":"75. Section 4 of the principal Act is amended by inserting after\nsubsection (2) the following subsections:\n \"(3) For the avoidance of doubt, the net profits referred to\nin subsection (2) shall not include any income derived from\nroyalty and other income derived from an intellectual property\nright if it is receivable as consideration for the commercial\nexploitation of that right.\n (4) Any income derived from intellectual property right\nreferred to in subsection (3) is subject to tax under the Income\nTax Act 1967.\n (5) For the purpose of this section, \"intellectual property\nright\" means a right arising from any patent, utility innovation\nand discovery, copyright, trade mark and service mark, industrial\ndesign, layout-design of integrated circuit, secret processes or\nformulae and know-how, geographical indication and the grant\nof protection of a plant variety, and other like rights, whether\nor not registered or registrable.\".\nDeletion of section 7"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A76","no":76,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 76"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter VI"},"text":{"en":"76. The principal Act is amended by deleting section 7.\nLaws of Malaysia40\nSubstitution of section 8"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A77","no":77,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 77"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter VI"},"text":{"en":"77. The principal Act is amended by substituting for section 8\nthe following section:\n\"Absence of basis period\n8. Where a Labuan entity carrying on a Labuan business\nactivity which is a Labuan trading activity does not have a\nbasis period for a year of assessment, the Director General\nmay direct that the basis period for that year of assessment\nand subsequent years of assessment to include a period or\nperiods (which may be of any period) as specified in the\ndirection.\".\nAmendment of section 8a"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A78","no":78,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 78"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter VI"},"text":{"en":"78. Subsection 8a(1) of the principal Act is amended by deleting\nthe words \", 7 or 8\".\nSubstitution of section 11"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A79","no":79,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 79"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter VI"},"text":{"en":"79. The principal Act is amended by substituting for section 11\nthe following section:\n\"Payment of tax\n11. A Labuan entity shall, at the time of filing of the statutory\ndeclaration and return of its profits for a year of assessment\nunder section 5, make full payment on account of—\n (a) tax to be charged for that year of assessment; or\n (b) tax to be charged for that year of assessment after\nreduction of rebate under section 8a.\".\nAmendment of section 12"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A80","no":80,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 80"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter VI"},"text":{"en":"80. Section 12 of the principal Act is amended by substituting\nfor the words \"paragraph 11 (a)\" the words \"section 11\".\nAct 812\nFinance 41\nAmendment of section 23"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A81","no":81,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 81"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter VI"},"text":{"en":"81. Paragraph 23 (b) of the principal Act is amended by deleting\nthe words \"7, 8 or\".\nAmendment of section 25"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A82","no":82,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 82"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter VI"},"text":{"en":"82. Section 25 of the principal Act is amended by deleting\nthe words \", 7, 8\".\nchapter  VII\nAMENDMENTS TO THE SERVICE TAX ACT 2018\nCommencement of amendments to the Service Tax Act 2018"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A83","no":83,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 83"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter VII"},"text":{"en":"83. This Chapter comes into operation on 1 January 2019.\nAmendment of section 2"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A84","no":84,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 84"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter VII"},"text":{"en":"84. The Service Tax Act 2018, which is referred to as the\n\"principal Act\" in this Chapter, is amended in section 2, by\ninserting after the definition of \"taxable service\" the following\ndefinition:\n ‘ \"imported taxable service\" means any taxable service\nacquired by any person in Malaysia from any person who is\noutside Malaysia;'.\nAmendment of section 7"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A85","no":85,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 85"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter VII"},"text":{"en":"85. The principal Act is amended by substituting for section 7\nthe following section:\n\"Imposition and scope of service tax\n7. A tax to be known as service tax shall be charged and\nlevied on—\n (a) any taxable service provided in Malaysia by a\nregistered person in carrying on his business; or\n (b) any imported taxable service.\".\nLaws of Malaysia42\nAmendment of section 9"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A86","no":86,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 86"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter VII"},"text":{"en":"86. Subsection 9(1) of the principal Act is amended—\n (a) in paragraph (b), by deleting the word \"or\" at the end of\nsubparagraph (iii);\n (b) by substituting for the full stop at the end of\nparagraph (c) the words \"; or\"; and\n (c) by inserting after paragraph (c) the following paragraph:\n \" (d) in the case of imported taxable service, the value\nof such imported taxable service shall be as\nprescribed.\".\nAmendment of section 11"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A87","no":87,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 87"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter VII"},"text":{"en":"87. Section 11 of the principal Act is amended by substituting\nfor subsection (1) the following subsection:\n \"(1) The service tax chargeable under section 7, shall\nbe due—\n (a) in the case of taxable service, at the time when payment\nis received for the service provided to the customer\nby the registered person; or\n (b) in the case of imported taxable service, at the time\nwhen the payment is made or invoice is received for\nthe service, whichever is the earlier.\".\nAmendment of section 24"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A88","no":88,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 88"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter VII"},"text":{"en":"88. Section 24 of the principal Act is amended—\n (a) in subsection (1)—\n (i) in paragraph (a), by deleting the word \"and\" at\nthe end of that paragraph; and\nAct 812\nFinance 43\n (ii) by inserting after paragraph (a) the following\nparagraph:\n \" (aa) all records of imported taxable service;\nand\";\n (b) by inserting after subsection (5) the following subsection:\n \"( 5a) This section shall also apply to any person\nother than a taxable person who, in carrying on his\nbusiness, acquires any imported taxable service.\"; and\n (c) in subsection (6), by substituting for the words \"or (4)\"\nthe words \", (4) or ( 5a)\".\nNew section 26a"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A89","no":89,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 89"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter VII"},"text":{"en":"89. The principal Act is amended by inserting after section 26\nthe following section:\n\"Furnishing of declaration and payment of service tax due\nand payable by person other than taxable person\n26a. (1) Any person other than a taxable person who, in\ncarrying on his business, acquires any imported taxable\nservice shall—\n (a) account for the service tax due in a declaration as\nmay be prescribed and the declaration shall be\nfurnished to the Director General; and\n (b) pay to the Director General the amount of service\ntax due and payable by him,\nnot later than the last day of the month following the end\nof the month in which the payment on the service has been\nmade by him or invoice is received by him.\nLaws of Malaysia44\n (2) Any person referred to in subsection (1) who—\n (a) contravenes subparagraph (1) (a); or\n (b)  furnishes an incorrect declaration,\ncommits an offence and shall, on conviction, be liable to a\nfine not exceeding fifty thousand ringgit or to imprisonment\nfor a term not exceeding three years or to both.\n (3) Any person referred to in subsection (1) who fails to\npay to the Director General the amount of service tax due\nand payable under paragraph (1) (b) commits an offence and\nshall, on conviction, be liable to a fine not exceeding fifty\nthousand ringgit or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding\nthree years or to both.\n (4) Where any service tax due and payable is not paid\nwholly or partly by any person referred to in subsection (1)\nafter the last day on which it is due and payable under\nsubsection (1) and no prosecution is instituted, the taxable\nperson shall pay—\n (a) for the first thirty-day period that the service tax is\nnot paid wholly or partly after the expiry of the\nperiod specified under subsection (1), a penalty of\nten per cent of the amount of service tax which\nremains unpaid;\n (b) for the second thirty-day period that the service tax\nis not paid wholly or partly after the expiry of the\nperiod specified under subsection (1), an additional\npenalty of fifteen per cent of the amount of service\ntax which remains unpaid; and\n (c) for the third thirty-day period that the service tax\nis not paid wholly or partly after the expiry of the\nperiod specified under subsection (1), an additional\npenalty of fifteen per cent of the amount of service\ntax which remains unpaid.\nAct 812\nFinance 45\n (5) Subject to subsection (7), prosecution for the offence\nunder subsection (3) may be instituted after the expiry of\nthe period specified in paragraph (4 )(c).\n (6) The court may order that the person referred\nto in subsection (1) who is convicted for the offence\nunder subsection (3) to pay the penalty as specified in\nsubsection (4).\n (7) No prosecution for the offence under subsection (3) shall\nbe instituted against any person referred to in subsection (1)\nwho has paid the amount of service tax due and payable, and\nthe penalty specified under subsection (4) within the period\nspecified in subsection (4).\".\nAmendment of section 27"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A90","no":90,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 90"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter VII"},"text":{"en":"90. Section 27 of the principal Act is amended—\n (a) by substituting for subsection (1) the following subsection:\n \"(1) Where—\n (a) any taxable person—\n (i) fails to apply for registration under\nsection 13;\n (ii) fails to furnish a return under section 26;\nor\n (iii) furnishes a return which appears to the\nDirector General to be incomplete or\nincorrect; or\n (b) any person other than a taxable person who,\nin carrying on his business, acquires any\nimported taxable service—\n (i) fails to furnish a declaration under\nsection 26a; or\n (ii) furnishes a declaration which appears to\nthe Director General to be incomplete\nor incorrect,\nLaws of Malaysia46\nthe Director General may assess to the best of his\njudgment the amount of service tax due and payable,\nand the penalty payable under subsection 26(8)\nor 26a(4), as the case may be, if any, by the taxable\nperson or person who is referred to in paragraph (1) (b)\nand shall forthwith notify him of the assessment in\nwriting.\";\n (b) in the national language text, in subsection (2), by deleting\nthe words \"kena cukai\";\n (c) in paragraph (4) (a), by substituting for the words\n\"paragraph (1)(a) or (b)\" the words \"subparagraph (1)(a)(i)\nor (ii);\n (d) in subsection (5)—\n (i) by substituting for paragraph (b) the following\nparagraph:\n \" (b) in the case of a taxable person, within\nthe taxable period during which the\nassessment could have been made, or\nin the case of the person referred to\nin paragraph (1) (b), within the period\nunder subsection 26 a(1),\"; and\n (ii) by deleting the word \"taxable\"; and\n (e) in subsection (6), by substituting for the words \"to any\ntaxable person under subsection (1), (2) or (5), it shall be\ndeemed to be an amount of service tax due and payable,\nand penalty payable, by him and may be recovered\naccordingly and the amount of service tax and penalty,\nif any, shall be paid by the taxable person, whether\nor not that taxable person\" the words \"pursuant to\nsubsection (1), (2) or (5), it shall be deemed to be an\namount of service tax due and payable, and penalty\npayable, by the person and may be recovered accordingly\nand the amount of service tax and penalty, if any, shall\nbe paid by the person, whether or not that person\".\nAct 812\nFinance 47\nchapter  VIII\nAMENDMENTS TO THE SALES TAX ACT 2018\nCommencement of amendments to the Sales Tax Act 2018"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A91","no":91,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 91"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter VIII"},"text":{"en":"91. This Chapter comes into operation on 1 January 2019 .\nAmendment of section 9"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A92","no":92,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 92"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter VIII"},"text":{"en":"92. The Sales Tax Act 2018, which is referred to as the \"principal\nAct\" in this Chapter, is amended in subsection 9(3) by deleting\nthe word \"registered\".\nAmendment of section 27"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A93","no":93,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 93"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter VIII"},"text":{"en":"93. Section 27 of the principal Act is amended—\n (a) in the national language text, in subsection (2), by deleting\nthe words \"kena cukai\";\n (b) in subsection (8)—\n (i) in paragraph (b), by inserting before the word\n\"within\" the words \"in the case of taxable\nperson,\"; and\n (ii) by deleting the word \"taxable\"; and\n (c) in subsection (9), by substituting for the words \"to any\ntaxable person under subsection (1), (2), (6) or (8),\nit shall be deemed to be an amount of sales tax due\nand payable, and penalty payable, by him and may be\nrecovered accordingly and the amount of sales tax and\npenalty, if any, shall be paid by the taxable person,\nwhether or not that taxable person\" the words \"pursuant to\nsubsection (1), (2), (6) or (8), it shall be deemed to be\nan amount of sales tax due and payable, and penalty\npayable, by the person and may be recovered accordingly\nand the amount of sales tax and penalty, if any, shall be\npaid by the person, whether or not that person\".\nLaws of Malaysia48\nAmendment of Part VI"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A94","no":94,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 94"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter VIII"},"text":{"en":"94. Part VI of the principal Act is amended in the\ntitle, by substituting for the words \"AND REMISSION\"\nthe words \", REMISSION AND DEDUCTION\".\nNew Section 41a"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A95","no":95,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 95"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter VIII"},"text":{"en":"95. The principal Act is amended by inserting after section 41\nthe following section:\n\"Deduction of sales tax\n41a. (1) Subject to subsection (2), the Minister may make\nregulations prescribing—\n (a) any amount of sales tax to be deducted in respect\nof taxable goods purchased by any registered\nmanufacturer;\n (b) any condition for the deduction; and\n (c) the form and manner of such deduction.\n (2) The deduction of sales tax under subsection (1) shall be\nmade on taxable goods which are raw materials, components\nor packaging materials used solely in the manufacturing of\ntaxable goods.\n (3) Where any registered manufacturer who has made\na deduction under subsection (1) fails to comply with any\nconditions to which the deduction relates, any sales tax that\nhas been the subject of the deduction shall become due and\npayable by the registered manufacturer on the date on which\nany of the conditions failed to be complied with.\".\nAmendment of section 82"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A96","no":96,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 96"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter VIII"},"text":{"en":"96. Subsection 82(6) of the principal Act is amended by substituting\nfor the words \"(6)\" the words \"(5)\".\nAct 812\nFinance 49\nNew section 88a"}},{"id":"MY-H588-A97","no":97,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 97"},"chapter":{"en":"chapter VIII"},"text":{"en":"97. The principal Act is amended by inserting after section 88\nthe following section:\n\"Improperly obtaining deduction of sales tax\n88 a. Any person who causes or attempts to cause the\ndeduction of sales tax under section 41a for himself or for any\nother person of any amount in excess of the amount properly\nso deductible for him or for that other person commits an\noffence and shall, on conviction, be liable—\n (a) to a fine not exceeding fifty thousand ringgit or to\nimprisonment for a term not exceeding three years\nor to both; and\n (b) to a penalty of two times the amount deducted in\nexcess of the amount properly so deductible.\"."}}],"pack":"my-13"};
  FT["MY-H5880"] = {"id":"MY-H5880","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 42/2022&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2022年道路交通（禁止使用道路）（联邦道路）（第4号）令","en":"ROAD TRANSPORT (PROHIBITION OF USE OF ROAD) (FEDERAL ROADS) (NO. 4) ORDER 2022","orig":"ROAD TRANSPORT (PROHIBITION OF USE OF ROAD) (FEDERAL ROADS) (NO. 4) ORDER 2022","ms":"Perintah Pengangkutan Jalan (Larangan Penggunaan Jalan) (Jalan Raya Persekutuan) (Bilangan 4) 2022","vi":"Lệnh về Vận tải đường bộ (Cấm sử dụng đường bộ) (Đường bộ liên bang) (số 4) năm 2022","th":"คำสั่งการขนส่งทางถนน (การห้ามใช้ถนน) (ทางหลวงสหพันธ์) (ฉบับที่ 4) ค.ศ. 2022","id":"Perintah Angkutan Jalan (Larangan Penggunaan Jalan) (Jalan Raya Federal) (Nomor 4) Tahun 2022"},"level":"regulation","category":"04_劳工与行政法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA42","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2022","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\04_劳工与行政法\\2022_P.U.(A)42-2022_ROAD TRANSPORT (PROHIBITION OF USE OF ROAD) (FEDERAL ROADS) (NO. 4) ORDER 2022.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H5880-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Pengangkutan Jalan\n\n(Larangan Penggunaan Jalan) (Jalan Persekutuan) (No. 4) 2022.\n\n(2) Perintah ini mula berkuat kuasa pada 7 Mac 2022.\n\nLarangan"}},{"id":"MY-H5880-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Pemanduan kenderaan di atas bahagian jalan yang dinyatakan dalam ruang (1)\n\nJadual Pertama sebagaimana yang ditunjukkan dalam peta dalam Jadual Kedua, selain di\n\natas jalan arah yang dinyatakan dalam ruang (2) Jadual Pertama, bagi tempoh yang\n\ndinyatakan dalam ruang (3) Jadual Pertama, dilarang.\n\nJADUAL PERTAMA\n\n(1)\n\nJalan yang baginya\n\nLarangan Terpakai\n\n(2)\n\nJalan Arah\n\n(3)\n\nTempoh Larangan\n\nSebahagian Laluan 1279,\n\nJalan Jelai Gemas 1-4\n\nbermula dari seksyen 3.10\n\nhingga seksyen 3.20\n\nsebagaimana yang\n\nditunjukkan dalam peta\n\ndalam Jadual Kedua\n\nKenderaan dari jalan utama\n\nJelai Gemas 1-4 ke Felda Jelai 2\n\ndan sebaliknya hendaklah\n\nmenggunakan jalan alternatif\n\nsebagaimana yang ditunjukkan\n\ndalam peta dalam Jadual Kedua\n\n7 Mac 2022 hingga\n\n6 Mac 2023\n\nJADUAL KEDUA\n\nDibuat 2 Mac 2022\n\n[KKR.100-1/2/79 Jld.2; PN(PU2)460/Jld. 115]\n\nDATO' SRI HAJI FADILLAH BIN HAJI YUSOF\n\nMenteri Kanan Kerja Raya\n\nROAD TRANSPORT ACT 1987\n\nROAD TRANSPORT (PROHIBITION OF USE OF ROAD)\n\n(FEDERAL ROADS) (NO. 4) ORDER 2022\n\nWHEREAS by P.U. (B) 97/2022 published on 15 February 2022, notice was given of the\n\nintention to make an order under section 70 of the Road Transport Act 1987 [Act 333]:\n\nAND WHEREAS no objection was received by the Senior Minister of Works against\n\nthe making of such order:\n\nNOW THEREFORE, in exercise of the powers conferred by section 70 of the Act,\n\nthe Senior Minister of Works, after taking into consideration the matters referred to in\n\nsubsection 70(2) of the Act, makes the following order:\n\nCitation and commencement\n\n1. (1) This order may be cited as the Road Transport (Prohibition of Use of\n\nRoad) (Federal Roads) (No. 4) Order 2022.\n\n(2) This Order comes into operation on 7 March 2022.\n\nProhibition\n\n2. The driving of vehicles on the part of the road as specified in column (1) of the\n\nFirst Schedule as shown on the map in the Second Schedule, otherwise than on the routes\n\nspecified in column (2) of the First Schedule, for the period specified in column (3) of the\n\nFirst Schedule, is prohibited.\n\nFIRST SCHEDULE\n\n(1)\n\nRoad to which\n\nProhibition Applies\n\n(2)\n\nRoutes\n\n(3)\n\nProhibition Period\n\nPart of Route 1279,\n\nJelai Gemas 1-4 Road\n\nstarting from section 3.10\n\nto section 3.20 as shown\n\non the map in the\n\nSecond Schedule\n\nVehicles from Jelai Gemas 1-4\n\nmain road to Felda Jelai 2 and\n\nvice versa shall use the\n\nalternative road as shown on the\n\nmap in the Second Schedule\n\n7 March 2022 to\n\n6 March 2023\n\nSECOND SCHEDULE\n\nMade 2 March 2022\n\n[KKR.110-1/2/79 Jld.2; PN(PU2)460/Jld. 115]\n\nDATO' SRI HAJI FADILLAH BIN HAJI YUSOF\n\nSenior Minister of Works"}}],"pack":"my-13"};
  FT["MY-H5881"] = {"id":"MY-H5881","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 42/2024&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":14,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2024年陆路公共交通（终端发牌）（车站与交通枢纽）条例","en":"LAND PUBLIC TRANSPORT (TERMINAL LICENSING) (STATION AND TRANSPORT HUB) REGULATIONS 2024","orig":"LAND PUBLIC TRANSPORT (TERMINAL LICENSING) (STATION AND TRANSPORT HUB) REGULATIONS 2024","ms":"Peraturan Pengangkutan Awam Darat (Pelesenan Terminal) (Stesen dan Hab Pengangkutan) 2024","vi":"Quy định về Vận tải công cộng đường bộ (Cấp phép bến bãi) (Ga và đầu mối giao thông) năm 2024","th":"ข้อบังคับการขนส่งสาธารณะทางบก (การออกใบอนุญาตสถานีรับส่ง) (สถานีและศูนย์กลางการขนส่ง) ค.ศ. 2024","id":"Peraturan Angkutan Umum Darat (Perizinan Terminal) (Stasiun dan Simpul Transportasi) Tahun 2024"},"level":"regulation","category":"04_劳工与行政法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA42","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2024","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 14 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\04_劳工与行政法\\2024_P.U.(A)42-2024_LAND PUBLIC TRANSPORT (TERMINAL LICENSING) (STATION AND TRANSPORT HUB) REGULATIONS 2024.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H5881-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. Nama dan permulaan kuat kuasa"}},{"id":"MY-H5881-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Pemakaian"}},{"id":"MY-H5881-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"ms":"3. Tafsiran\n\nBAHAGIAN II\n\nPELESENAN"}},{"id":"MY-H5881-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"ms":"4. Permohonan bagi lesen"}},{"id":"MY-H5881-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"ms":"5. Pemeriksaan terminal"}},{"id":"MY-H5881-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6"},"text":{"ms":"6. Bentuk lesen"}},{"id":"MY-H5881-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7"},"text":{"ms":"7. Sijil lesen terminal dan sijil penarafan gred terminal"}},{"id":"MY-H5881-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8"},"text":{"ms":"8. Pembaharuan lesen"}},{"id":"MY-H5881-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9"},"text":{"ms":"9. Pengubahan lesen"}},{"id":"MY-H5881-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10"},"text":{"ms":"10. Salinan pendua lesen"}},{"id":"MY-H5881-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11"},"text":{"ms":"11. Larangan pemindahan lesen terminal\n\nBAHAGIAN III\n\nCAJ TERMINAL"}},{"id":"MY-H5881-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 12"},"text":{"ms":"12. Caj terminal\n\nBAHAGIAN IV\n\nPEMATUHAN"}},{"id":"MY-H5881-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 13"},"text":{"ms":"13. Penggunaan selamat dan penyenggaraan"}},{"id":"MY-H5881-A14","no":14,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 14"},"text":{"ms":"14. Penyimpanan rekod\n\nJADUAL PERTAMA\n\nJADUAL KEDUA\n\nJADUAL KETIGA\n\nAKTA PENGANGKUTAN AWAM DARAT 2010\n\nPERATURAN-PERATURAN PENGANGKUTAN AWAM DARAT\n\n(PELESENAN TERMINAL) (STESEN DAN PUSAT PENGANGKUTAN) 2024\n\nPADA menjalankan kuasa yang diberikan oleh perenggan 252(1)(a), (b), (i), (r), (s), (ti),\n\n(tl), (tm), (tn), (ty), (tak) dan subperenggan (tb)(i) Akta Pengangkutan Awam Darat 2010\n\n[Akta 715], Menteri membuat peraturan-peraturan yang berikut:\n\nBAHAGIAN I\n\nPERMULAAN\n\nNama dan permulaan kuat kuasa\n\n1. (1) Peraturan-peraturan ini bolehlah dinamakan Peraturan-Peraturan\n\nPengangkutan Awam Darat (Pelesenan Terminal) (Stesen dan Pusat\n\nPengangkutan) 2024.\n\n(2) Peraturan-Peraturan ini mula berkuat kuasa pada 6 Februari 2024.\n\nPemakaian\n\n2. Peraturan-Peraturan ini hendaklah terpakai bagi pemilik terminal,\n\npemegang lesen terminal dan pengguna terminal yang berhubungan dengan\n\nstesen tunggal atau pelbagai modal dan pusat pengangkutan yang dikhususkan bagi\n\npengangkutan awam darat.\n\nTafsiran\n\n3. Dalam Peraturan-Peraturan ini, melainkan jika konteksnya menghendaki makna\n\nyang lain—\n\n\"caj terminal\" ertinya fi yang boleh dikenakan oleh pemegang lesen terminal\n\nmengikut gred terminal sebagaimana yang ditetapkan dalam Jadual Kedua;\n\n\"fi lesen\" ertinya fi tahunan yang dikenakan kepada pemegang lesen terminal\n\nmengikut kategori sebagaimana yang ditetapkan dalam Jadual Pertama;\n\n\"gred terminal\" ertinya gred sebagaimana yang ditentukan oleh Ketua Pengarah\n\nPengangkutan Awam Darat dalam lesen berdasarkan kemudahan, fasiliti dan tahap\n\nperkhidmatan yang disediakan di stesen dan pusat pengangkutan bagi tujuan penentuan\n\ncaj terminal;\n\n\"kategori terminal\" ertinya kategori terminal sebagaimana yang ditentukan oleh\n\nKetua Pengarah Pengangkutan Awam Darat dalam lesen mengikut purata harian\n\njumlah penumpang dalam setahun atau purata harian jumlah kemasukan kenderaan\n\nperkhidmatan awam dan kenderaan pelancongan ke terminal dalam setahun\n\nsebagaimana yang ditetapkan dalam Jadual Pertama;\n\n\"operasi terminal\" ertinya aktiviti mengambil dan menurunkan penumpang,\n\naktiviti perniagaan, aktiviti masuk dan keluar orang di terminal dan lain-lain aktiviti\n\ndi dalam kawasan terminal termasuklah—\n\n(i) kutipan caj terminal;\n\n(ii) pengurusan dan pengawalseliaan operasi terminal;\n\n(iii) pembersihan dan penyenggaraan; dan\n\n(iv) sistem keselamatan dan sekuriti;\n\n\"pemilik terminal\" ertinya pemilik bangunan yang bangunannya digunakan\n\nsepenuhnya atau sebahagiannya untuk operasi terminal;\n\n\"pengguna terminal\" ertinya mana-mana orang yang berada di sekitar kawasan\n\nterminal termasuk penumpang.\n\nBAHAGIAN II\n\nPELESENAN\n\nPermohonan bagi lesen\n\n4. (1) Permohonan bagi suatu lesen terminal oleh seseorang yang berniat untuk\n\nmenjalankan operasi terminal hendaklah dibuat kepada Ketua Pengarah Pengangkutan\n\nAwam Darat mengikut apa-apa cara sebagaimana yang ditentukan oleh Ketua Pengarah\n\nPengangkutan Awam Darat.\n\n(2) Permohonan di bawah subperaturan (1) hendaklah—\n\n(a) dibuat dalam borang sebagaimana yang ditentukan oleh\n\nKetua Pengarah Pengangkutan Awam Darat;\n\n(b) disertakan dengan fi sebagaimana yang ditetapkan dalam\n\nJadual Pertama; dan\n\n(c) disertakan dengan apa-apa maklumat atau dokumen sebagaimana\n\nyang ditentukan oleh Ketua Pengarah Pengangkutan Awam Darat.\n\n(3) Selepas menimbangkan permohonan di bawah subperaturan (1),\n\nKetua Pengarah Pengangkutan Awam Darat boleh—\n\n(a) meluluskan permohonan itu dan mengeluarkan lesen terminal\n\nkepada pemohon tertakluk kepada apa-apa syarat yang\n\ndifikirkannya patut; atau\n\n(b) menolak permohonan itu dengan menyatakan alasan bagi\n\npenolakan itu.\n\nPemeriksaan terminal\n\n5. (1) Sebelum permohonan diluluskan di bawah peraturan 4, mana-mana\n\npegawai pengangkutan awam darat yang dilantik dan diberi kuasa oleh Ketua Pengarah\n\nPengangkutan Awam Darat, hendaklah pada bila-bila masa, menjalankan pemeriksaan\n\ndi terminal.\n\n(2) Pemegang lesen terminal hendaklah memberi akses penuh untuk\n\nmemasuki terminal kepada mana-mana pegawai pengangkutan awam darat untuk\n\nmenjalankan pemeriksaan.\n\n(3) Setelah pemeriksaan dibuat, Ketua Pengarah Pengangkutan Awam Darat\n\nhendaklah menentukan kategori terminal dan gred terminal.\n\n(4) Dalam hal keadaan Ketua Pengarah Pengangkutan Awam Darat\n\nmengelaskan semula gred terminal kepada gred yang lebih rendah, Ketua Pengarah\n\nPengangkutan Awam Darat hendaklah memberikan notis bertulis kepada pemegang\n\nlesen terminal mengarahkan pemegang lesen terminal itu menambah baik\n\ntahap perkhidmatan selaras dengan gred asalnya.\n\nBentuk lesen\n\n6. Suatu lesen terminal yang dikeluarkan oleh Ketua Pengarah Pengangkutan Awam\n\nDarat di bawah subperaturan 4(4) hendaklah mengandungi—\n\n(a) sijil lesen terminal;\n\n(b) sijil penarafan gred terminal; dan\n\n(c) syarat lesen terminal.\n\nSijil lesen terminal dan sijil penarafan gred terminal\n\n7. (1) Sijil lesen terminal dan sijil penarafan gred terminal hendaklah\n\nmengandungi maklumat sebagaimana yang ditetapkan dalam Jadual Ketiga.\n\n(2) Bagi maksud penentuan sesuatu gred terminal, Ketua Pengarah\n\nPengangkutan Awam Darat hendaklah mengambil kira tahap kemudahan seperti yang\n\nberikut:\n\n(a) sistem pentiketan dan informasi;\n\n(b) sistem pengurusan aliran trafik bagi kenderaan dan pengguna\n\nterminal;\n\n(c) sistem keselamatan; dan\n\n(d) keselesaan pengguna terminal.\n\nPembaharuan lesen\n\n8. (1) Suatu permohonan bagi pembaharuan lesen terminal oleh pemegang lesen\n\nterminal hendaklah dibuat sekurang-kurangnya sembilan puluh hari sebelum\n\ntarikh habis tempoh lesen terminal itu dan hendaklah—\n\n(a) dibuat dalam borang sebagaimana yang ditentukan oleh\n\nKetua Pengarah Pengangkutan Awam Darat;\n\n(b) disertakan dengan fi sebagaimana yang ditetapkan dalam\n\nJadual Pertama; dan\n\n(c) disertakan dengan apa-apa maklumat dan dokumen sebagaimana\n\nyang ditentukan oleh Ketua Pengarah Pengangkutan Awam Darat.\n\n(2) Sekiranya suatu permohonan untuk membaharui lesen terminal\n\ndiluluskan, Ketua Pengarah Pengangkutan Awam Darat hendaklah mengeluarkan\n\nlesen terminal baharu kepada pemohon.\n\nPengubahan lesen\n\n9. (1) Sekiranya terdapat apa-apa perubahan seperti yang berikut,\n\npemegang lesen terminal hendaklah membuat permohonan pengubahan lesen terminal:\n\n(a) nama terminal;\n\n(b) pegangan ekuiti syarikat;\n\n(c) keanggotaan ahli lembaga pengarah syarikat;\n\n(d) nama dan alamat syarikat;\n\n(e) waktu operasi terminal;\n\n(f) perubahan kepada pelan lantai; dan\n\n(g) perubahan kepada gred terminal.\n\n(2) Permohonan bagi pengubahan lesen terminal oleh pemegang lesen\n\nterminal hendaklah—\n\n(a) dibuat dalam borang sebagaimana yang ditentukan oleh\n\nKetua Pengarah Pengangkutan Awam Darat;\n\n(b) disertakan dengan fi sebagaimana yang ditetapkan dalam\n\nJadual Pertama; dan\n\n(c) disertakan dengan apa-apa maklumat dan dokumen seperti yang\n\nberikut:\n\n(i) justifikasi pengubahan; dan\n\n(ii) data dan maklumat sokongan bagi pengubahan.\n\n(3) Sekiranya permohonan bagi pengubahan lesen terminal diluluskan,\n\nKetua Pengarah Pengangkutan Awam Darat hendaklah mengeluarkan lesen terminal\n\nyang baharu kepada pemohon dan Ketua Pengarah Pengangkutan Awam Darat boleh\n\nmengenakan apa-apa syarat yang difikirkannya patut.\n\n(4) Sekiranya terdapat perubahan yang berhubungan dengan kategori dan\n\ngred terminal kepada kemudahan yang disediakan sebagaimana yang dinyatakan dalam\n\nperaturan 5, Ketua Pengarah Pengangkutan Awam Darat boleh, pada bila-bila masa,\n\nmemeriksa semula terminal.\n\nSalinan pendua lesen\n\n10. (1) Jika lesen yang dikeluarkan oleh Ketua Pengarah Pengangkutan Awam\n\nDarat di bawah Peraturan-Peraturan ini hilang, cacat, rosak atau musnah atau atas sebab\n\nmunasabah yang lain, suatu permohonan untuk salinan pendua lesen oleh\n\npemegang lesen terminal hendaklah—\n\n(a) dibuat dalam borang sebagaimana yang ditentukan oleh\n\nKetua Pengarah Pengangkutan Awam Darat;\n\n(b) disertakan dengan fi sebagaimana yang ditetapkan dalam\n\nJadual Pertama; dan\n\n(c) disertakan dengan apa-apa maklumat dan dokumen sebagaimana\n\nyang ditentukan oleh Ketua Pengarah Pengangkutan Awam Darat.\n\n(2) Selepas menimbangkan permohonan itu, Ketua Pengarah Pengangkutan\n\nAwam Darat boleh—\n\n(a) meluluskan permohonan itu dan mengeluarkan kepada pemohon\n\nsalinan pendua lesen dengan perkataan \"PENDUA\" diendorskan\n\npada salinan lesen itu; atau\n\n(b) menolak permohonan itu dengan menyatakan alasan bagi penolakan\n\nitu.\n\nLarangan pemindahan lesen terminal\n\n11. Suatu lesen terminal yang dikeluarkan di bawah peraturan 4 tidak boleh\n\ndipindahkan atau diserahhakkan kepada mana-mana orang lain.\n\nBAHAGIAN III\n\nCAJ TERMINAL\n\nCaj terminal\n\n12. (1) Pemegang lesen terminal boleh mengenakan caj terminal sebagaimana\n\nyang ditetapkan dalam Jadual Kedua.\n\n(2) Caj terminal hendaklah ditetapkan berdasarkan penarafan gred terminal\n\nyang telah diberikan oleh Ketua Pengarah Pengangkutan Awam Darat\n\ndalam lesen terminal.\n\n(3) Ketua Pengarah Pengangkutan Awam Darat boleh, atas sebab kepentingan\n\nawam, melalui notis bertulis, mengarahkan pemegang lesen terminal untuk mengubah\n\ncaj terminal yang dinyatakan dalam syarat lesen terminal dalam masa tujuh hari\n\ndari tarikh notis bertulis itu.\n\nBAHAGIAN IV\n\nPEMATUHAN\n\nPenggunaan selamat dan penyenggaraan\n\n13. Pemegang lesen terminal hendaklah memastikan—\n\n(a) terminal bersih dan semua kemudahan yang disediakan berfungsi dan\n\nselamat untuk digunakan dan memastikan kerja-kerja pembersihan dan\n\npenyenggaraan dijalankan mengikut jadual;\n\n(b) operasi terminal berjalan lancar dan selamat;\n\n(c) sistem teknologi terminal mampu mengawal selia aktiviti pengguna\n\nterminal dan kenderaan;\n\n(d) terma dan syarat lesen terminal berdasarkan gred yang telah ditentukan\n\noleh Ketua Pengarah Pengangkutan Awam Darat dipatuhi; dan\n\n(e) semua dokumen, rekod dan laporan berkaitan dengan kemudahan,\n\nperalatan, penyenggaraan, bangunan dan operasi terminal disimpan\n\ndengan baik dan dikemukakan kepada Ketua Pengarah Pengangkutan\n\nAwam Darat dalam apa-apa tempoh dan mengikut apa-apa cara\n\nsebagaimana yang ditentukan oleh Ketua Pengarah Pengangkutan Awam\n\nDarat.\n\nPenyimpanan rekod\n\n14. (1) Pemegang lesen terminal hendaklah menyimpan rekod dan dokumen\n\nyang berikut:\n\n(a) pelan lantai terminal dan lukisan siap bina yang disahkan oleh\n\narkitek profesional;\n\n(b) rekod penyengaraan terminal;\n\n(c) rekod operasi terminal termasuk data kenderaan, penumpang, trip,\n\npentiketan, kesalahan dan lain-lain rekod operasi yang ditentukan\n\noleh Ketua Pengarah Pengangkutan Awam Darat dari semasa\n\nke semasa;\n\n(d) rekod dalam sistem pengurusan terminal; dan\n\n(e) rekod lain sebagaimana yang ditentukan oleh Ketua Pengarah\n\nPengangkutan Awam Darat.\n\n(2) Apabila diminta oleh Ketua Pengarah Pengangkutan Awam Darat,\n\npemegang lesen terminal hendaklah mengemukakan dokumen yang disebut dalam\n\nsubperaturan (1) dalam tempoh tujuh hari.\n\nJADUAL PERTAMA\n\n[Peraturan 4, 8, 9 dan 10]\n\nFI LESEN\n\n(1)\n\nHal Perkara\n\n(2)\n\nKadar Fi\n\n(RM)\n\nFi permohonan 50.00\n\nFi pembaharuan 50.00\n\nFi pengubahan 50.00\n\nFi lesen\n\n(a) Kategori Terminal 1\n\n10,000 penumpang ke atas\n\natau\n\n3,000 kenderaan ke atas\n\n14,000.00\n\n(b) Kategori Terminal 2\n\n5,000 hingga 9,999\n\npenumpang\n\natau\n\n1,000 hingga 2,999\n\nkenderaan\n\n7,000.00\n\n(c) Kategori Terminal 3\n\n1,000 hingga 4,999\n\npenumpang\n\natau\n\n500 hingga 999 kenderaan\n\n3,000.00\n\n(d) Kategori Terminal 4\n\n999 penumpang ke bawah\n\natau\n\n1,000.00\n\n499 kenderaan dan\n\nke bawah\n\nFi pengeluaran\n\n(i) Sijil lesen 30.00\n\n(ii) Sijil penarafan gred terminal 30.00\n\n(iii) Syarat-syarat lesen Percuma\n\nFi salinan pendua\n\nlesen\n\n(i) Sijil lesen 100.00\n\n(ii) Sijil penarafan gred terminal 100.00\n\n(iii) Syarat-syarat lesen 50.00\n\nJADUAL KEDUA\n\n[Peraturan 12]\n\nCAJ TERMINAL\n\n(1)\n\nJenis Caj\n\n(2)\n\nCaj Terminal bagi Terminal dengan\n\nSistem Penjualan Tiket Berpusat\n\n(RM)\n\n(3)\n\nCaj Terminal bagi Terminal\n\ntanpa Sistem Penjualan\n\nTiket Berpusat\n\n(RM)\n\nGred A Gred B Gred C Gred B Gred C\n\nCaj tiket kepada\n\npengendali berlesen\n\nbas ekspres\n\n10%\n\ndaripada\n\nharga tiket\n\natau\n\n5.00 yang\n\nmana lebih\n\nrendah\n\n10%\n\ndaripada\n\nharga tiket\n\natau\n\n3.00 yang\n\nmana lebih\n\nrendah\n\n10%\n\ndaripada\n\nharga tiket\n\natau\n\n2.00 yang\n\nmana lebih\n\nrendah\n\ntiada tiada\n\nCaj masuk bas\n\nkepada pengendali\n\nberlesen—\n\n(a) bas ekspres\n\n(b) bas\n\nberhenti-henti\n\n(c) lain-lain\n\n10.00\n\n3.00\n\n15.00\n\n7.00\n\n2.00\n\n10.00\n\n5.00\n\n1.00\n\n7.00\n\n7.00\n\n2.00\n\n10.00\n\n5.00\n\n1.00\n\n7.00\n\nCaj masuk bas\n\nkepada pemegang\n\nlesen terminal bas\n\npersiaran\n\n15.00 10.00 7.00 10.00 7.00\n\nCaj fasiliti kepada\n\npenumpang\n\n1.00 0.70 0.50 tiada tiada\n\nJADUAL KETIGA\n\n[Peraturan 7]\n\nSIJIL LESEN TERMINAL DAN SIJIL PENARAFAN GRED TERMINAL\n\nSijil lesen terminal\n\n1. Sijil lesen terminal hendaklah mengandungi maklumat yang berikut:\n\n(a) kategori terminal;\n\n(b) nama pemegang lesen terminal;\n\n(c) nama terminal;\n\n(d) alamat terminal;\n\n(e) gred terminal; dan\n\n(f) tempoh lesen terminal.\n\nSijil penarafan gred terminal\n\n2. Sijil penarafan gred terminal hendaklah mengandungi maklumat seperti yang\n\nberikut:\n\n(a) nama terminal;\n\n(b) penarafan gred terminal; dan\n\n(c) tempoh sijil.\n\nDibuat 2 Februari 2024\n\n[MOT.BD.(S).600-2/21 Jld. 3(3); PN(PU2)692/IV]\n\nLOKE SIEW FOOK\n\nMenteri Pengangkutan\n\nLAND PUBLIC TRANSPORT ACT 2010\n\nLAND PUBLIC TRANSPORT (TERMINAL LICENSING) (STATION AND TRANSPORT HUB)\n\nREGULATIONS 2024\n\nARRANGEMENT OF REGULATION\n\nPART I\n\nPRELIMINARY\n\nRegulation\n\n1. Citation and commencement\n\n2. Application\n\n3. Interpretation\n\nPART II\n\nLICENSING\n\n4. Application for licence\n\n5. Inspection of terminal\n\n6. Form of licence\n\n7. Terminal licence certificate and terminal grade rating certificate\n\n8. Renewal of licence\n\n9. Variation of licence\n\n10. Duplicate copy of licence\n\n11. Prohibition of transfer of terminal licence\n\nPART III\n\nTERMINAL CHARGE\n\n12. Terminal charge\n\nPART IV\n\nCOMPLIANCE\n\n13. Safety of use and maintenance\n\n14. Record keeping\n\nFIRST SCHEDULE\n\nSECOND SCHEDULE\n\nTHIRD SCHEDULE\n\nLAND PUBLIC TRANSPORT ACT 2010\n\nLAND PUBLIC TRANSPORT (TERMINAL LICENSING) (STATION AND TRANSPORT HUB)\n\nREGULATIONS 2024\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by paragraphs 252(1)(a),(b),(i),(r), (s),(ti),(tl),(tm),\n\n(tn), (ty), (tak) and subparagraph (tb)(i) of the Land Public Transport Act 2010 [Act 715],\n\nthe Minister makes the following regulations:\n\nPART I\n\nPRELIMINARY\n\nCitation and commencement\n\n1. (1) These regulations may be cited as the Land Public Transport\n\n(Terminal Licensing) (Station and Transport Hub) Regulations 2024.\n\n(2) These Regulations come into operation on 6 February 2024.\n\nApplication\n\n2. These Regulations shall apply to terminal owner, terminal licensee and\n\nterminal user relating to a single or multi-modal station and transport hub dedicated to\n\nland public transport.\n\nInterpretation\n\n3. In these Regulations, unless the context otherwise requires—\n\n\"terminal charge\" means fees that may be imposed by a terminal licensee\n\nin accordance with the terminal grade as prescribed in the Second Schedule;\n\n\"licence fee\" means the annual fee imposed to the terminal licensee in accordance\n\nwith the category as prescribed in the First Schedule;\n\n\"terminal grade\" means the grade as may be determined by the Director General\n\nof Land Public Transport in the licence based on the amenities, facilities and level of\n\nservices provided at the station and transport hub for the purpose of determining\n\nterminal charge;\n\n\"terminal category\" means the category of terminal as may be determined by\n\nthe Director General of Land Public Transport in the licence according to the average daily\n\nnumber of passengers in a year or the average daily number of the entry of public service\n\nvehicles and tourism vehicles to the terminal in a year as prescribed in the First Schedule;\n\n\"terminal operation\" means the activity of embarking and disembarking\n\npassengers, business activity, the entry and exit of people activity in the terminal and\n\nother activities in the terminal area including—\n\n(i) collection of terminal charge;\n\n(ii) management and regulation of terminal operation;\n\n(iii) cleaning and maintenance; and\n\n(iv) safety and security system;\n\n\"terminal owner\" means the owner of the building whose building is used in whole\n\nor in part for terminal operation;\n\n\"terminal user\" means any person that is in the vicinity of the terminal area\n\nincluding passengers.\n\nPART II\n\nLICENSING\n\nApplication for licence\n\n4. (1) An application for a terminal licence by any person who intends to carry on\n\nthe terminal operation shall be made to the Director General of Land Public Transport\n\nin such manner as may be determined by the Director General of Land Public Transport.\n\n(2) The application under subregulation (1) shall be—\n\n(a) made in an application form as may be determined by\n\nthe Director General of Land Public Transport;\n\n(b) accompanied by a fee as prescribed in the First Schedule; and\n\n(c) accompanied by any information or document as may be\n\ndetermined by the Director General of Land Public Transport.\n\n(3) After considering the application under subregulation (1),\n\nthe Director General of Land Public Transport may—\n\n(a) approve the application and issue the terminal licence\n\nto the applicant subject to any condition as he thinks fit; or\n\n(b) refuse the application by stating the grounds for refusal.\n\nInspection of terminal\n\n5. (1) Before the application is approved under regulation 4, any land public\n\ntransport officer appointed and duly authorized by the Director General of Land Public\n\nTransport, shall at any time, conduct an inspection at the terminal.\n\n(2) The terminal licensee shall provide full access to enter the terminal\n\nto any land public transport officer to carry out the inspection.\n\n(3) After the inspection has been made, the Director General\n\nof Land Public Transport shall determine the category and grade of the terminal.\n\n(4) In circumstances where the Director General of Land Public Transport\n\nreclassifies the terminal grade to a lower grade, the Director General of Land Public\n\nTransport shall give written notice to the terminal licensee instructing the terminal\n\nlicensee to improve the service level to be consistent with the original grade.\n\nForm of licence\n\n6. A terminal licence issued by the Director General of Land Public Transport\n\nunder subregulation 4(4) shall consist of—\n\n(a) a terminal licence certificate;\n\n(b) a terminal grade rating certificate; and\n\n(c) terminal licence condition.\n\nTerminal licence certificate and terminal grade rating certificate\n\n7. (1) The terminal licence certificate and the terminal grade rating certificate\n\nshall contain the information as prescribed in the Third Schedule.\n\n(2) For the purpose of determining a terminal grade, the Director General\n\nof Land Public Transport shall take into account the level of facilities\n\nas follows:\n\n(a) ticketing and information system;\n\n(b) traffic flow management system for vehicle and terminal user;\n\n(c) security system; and\n\n(d) terminal user comfort.\n\nRenewal of licence\n\n8. (1) An application for a renewal of the terminal licence by a terminal licensee\n\nshall be made at least ninety days before the date of expiry of the terminal licence and\n\nshall be—\n\n(a) made in the form as may be determined by the Director General of\n\nLand Public Transport;\n\n(b) accompanied by a fee as prescribed in the First Schedule; and\n\n(c) accompanied by any information and document as may be\n\ndetermined by the Director General of Land Public Transport.\n\n(2) If the application for renewal of the terminal licence is approved,\n\nthe Director General of Land Public Transport shall issue a new terminal licence\n\nto the applicant.\n\nVariation of licence\n\n9. (1) If changes occur in any of the following, a terminal licensee shall apply for\n\nvariation of the terminal licence:\n\n(a) name of the terminal;\n\n(b) the company's equity holding;\n\n(c) membership of the company's board of director;\n\n(d) name and address of the company;\n\n(e) terminal operating hours;\n\n(f) changes to floor plan; and\n\n(g) changes to terminal grade.\n\n(2) An application for the variation of terminal licence by a terminal licensee\n\nshall be—\n\n(a) made in the form as may be determined by the Director General\n\nof Land Public Transport;\n\n(b) accompanied by a fee as prescribed in the First Schedule; and\n\n(c) accompanied by any information and document as follows:\n\n(i) justification of the variation; and\n\n(ii) supporting data and information for the variation.\n\n(3) If the application for variation of the terminal licence is approved,\n\nthe Director General of Land Public Transport shall issue a new terminal licence\n\nto the applicant and the Director General of Land Public Transport may impose such\n\nconditions as he thinks fit.\n\n(4) If there is any change to the facilities relating to the category and grade\n\nof the terminal provided as specified in regulation 5, the Director General of Land Public\n\nTransport may, at any time, re-inspect the terminal.\n\nDuplicate copy of licence\n\n10. (1) If the licence issued by the Director General of Land Public Transport under\n\nthese Regulations is lost, mutilated, defaced or destroyed or for other reasonable reasons,\n\nan application for the duplicate copy of a licence by the terminal licensee shall be—\n\n(a) made in the form as may be determined by the Director General\n\nof Land Public Transport;\n\n(b) accompanied by a fee as prescribed in the First Schedule; and\n\n(c) accompanied by any information and document as may be\n\ndetermined by the Director General of Land Public Transport.\n\n(2) After considering the application, the Director General of Land Public\n\nTransport may—\n\n(a) approve the application and issue to the applicant a duplicate copy\n\nof licence with the word \"DUPLICATE\" endorsed on the copy\n\nof the licence; or\n\n(b) refuse the application by stating the grounds for refusal.\n\nProhibition of transfer of terminal licence\n\n11. A terminal licence issued under regulation 4 shall not be transferred or assigned\n\nto any other person.\n\nPART III\n\nTERMINAL CHARGE\n\nTerminal charge\n\n12. (1) A terminal licensee may impose terminal charge as prescribed\n\nin the Second Schedule.\n\n(2) The terminal charge shall be prescribed based on the terminal grade rating\n\ngiven by the Director General of Land Public Transport in the terminal licence.\n\n(3) The Director General of Land Public Transport may, for reason\n\nof public interest, by a written notice, instruct the terminal licensee to vary\n\nthe terminal charge specified in the terminal licence conditions within seven days\n\nfrom the date of the written notice.\n\nPART IV\n\nCOMPLIANCE\n\nSafety of use and maintenance\n\n13. A terminal licensee shall ensure that—\n\n(a) the terminal is clean and all facilities provided are functional and safe\n\nto use and ensure cleaning and maintenance work is carried out\n\naccording to the schedule;\n\n(b) the terminal operation is carry out smoothly and safe;\n\n(c) the technology system of the terminal is capable of regulating the activities\n\nof terminal users and vehicles;\n\n(d) the terms and conditions of the terminal licence based on the grade\n\ndetermined by the Director General of Land Public Transport\n\nare complied with; and\n\n(e) all documents, records and reports in respect of facility, equipment,\n\nmaintenance, building and terminal operation are properly kept and\n\nsubmitted to the Director General of Land Public Transport within\n\nany period and in any manner as may be determined by\n\nthe Director General of Land Public Transport.\n\nRecord keeping\n\n14. (1) A terminal licensee shall keep the following records and documents:\n\n(a) terminal floor plan and completed drawings certified by\n\na professional architect;\n\n(b) terminal maintenance records;\n\n(c) terminal operation records including data on vehicles, passengers,\n\ntrip, ticketing, offences and other operational records specified by\n\nthe Director General of Land Public Transport from time to time;\n\n(d) records in the terminal management system; and\n\n(e) other records as may be determined by the Director General of\n\nLand Public Transport.\n\n(2) Upon request by the Director General of Land Public Transport,\n\nthe terminal licensee shall provide the documents referred to in subregulation (1)\n\nwithin seven days.\n\nFIRST SCHEDULE\n\n[Regulations 4, 8, 9 and 10]\n\nLICENCE FEE\n\n(1)\n\nSubject Matter\n\n(2)\n\nFee Rate\n\n(RM)\n\nApplication fee 50.00\n\nRenewal fee 50.00\n\nVariation fee 50.00\n\nLicence fee\n\n(a) Terminal 1 Category\n\n10,000 passengers and above\n\nor\n\n3,000 vehicles and above\n\n14,000.00\n\n(b) Terminal 2 Category\n\n5,000 to 9,999 passengers\n\nor\n\n1,000 to 2,999 vehicles\n\n7,000.00\n\n(c) Terminal 3 Category\n\n1,000 to 4,999 passengers\n\n or\n\n500 to 999 vehicles\n\n3,000.00\n\n(d) Terminal 4 Category\n\n999 passengers and below\n\nor\n\n499 vehicles and below\n\n1,000.00\n\nIssuance fee\n\n(i) Licence certificate 30.00\n\n(ii) Terminal grade rating\n\ncertificate 30.00\n\n(iii) Licence conditions Free\n\nDuplicate copy of\n\nlicence fee\n\n(i) Licence certificate 100.00\n\n(ii) Terminal grade rating\n\ncertificate 100.00\n\n(iii) Licence conditions 50.00\n\nSECOND SCHEDULE\n\n[Regulation 12]\n\nTERMINAL CHARGE\n\n(1)\n\nType of Charge\n\n(2)\n\nTerminal Charge for Terminal with\n\nCentralized Ticketing System\n\n(RM)\n\n(3)\n\nTerminal Charge for\n\nTerminal without\n\nCentralized Ticketing\n\nSystem\n\n(RM)\n\nGrade A Grade B Grade C Grade B Grade C\n\nTicket charged to\n\nlicensed\n\noperator of\n\nexpress bus\n\n10% from\n\nthe ticket\n\nprice\n\nor\n\n5.00\n\nwhichever is\n\nlower\n\n10% from\n\nthe ticket\n\nprice\n\nor\n\n3.00\n\nwhichever is\n\nlower\n\n10% from\n\nthe ticket\n\nprice\n\nor\n\n2.00\n\nwhichever is\n\nlower\n\nnone none\n\nBus entry charge\n\nto licensed\n\noperator\n\n(a) express bus\n\n(b) stage bus\n\n(c) other\n\n10.00\n\n3.00\n\n15.00\n\n7.00\n\n2.00\n\n10.00\n\n5.00\n\n1.00\n\n7.00\n\n7.00\n\n2.00\n\n10.00\n\n5.00\n\n1.00\n\n7.00\n\nBus entry charge\n\nto terminal\n\nlicensee of\n\nexcursion bus\n\n15.00 10.00 7.00 10.00 7.00\n\nFacility charge to\n\npassengers\n\n1.00 0.70 0.50 none none\n\nTHIRD SCHEDULE\n\n[Regulation 7]\n\nTERMINAL LICENCE CERTIFICATE AND TERMINAL GRADE RATING CERTIFICATE\n\nTerminal licence certificate\n\n1. The terminal licence certificate shall contain the following information:\n\n(a) category of the terminal;\n\n(b) name of the terminal licensee;\n\n(c) name of the terminal;\n\n(d) address of the terminal;\n\n(e) grade of the terminal; and\n\n(f) terminal licence period.\n\nTerminal grade rating certificate\n\n2. The terminal grade rating certificate shall contain the following information:\n\n(a) name of the terminal;\n\n(b) terminal grade rating; and\n\n(c) terminal licence period.\n\nMade 2 February 2024\n\n[MOT.BD.(S).600-2/21 Jld. 3(3); PN(PU2)692/IV]\n\nLOKE SIEW FOOK\n\nMinister of Transport"}}],"pack":"my-13"};
  FT["MY-H5882"] = {"id":"MY-H5882","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 42/2025&status=AMENDMENT","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":3,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2025年联邦道路（联邦土地发展局计划）（修正）令","en":"FEDERAL ROADS (FELDA SCHEME) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2025","orig":"FEDERAL ROADS (FELDA SCHEME) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2025","ms":"Perintah Jalan Raya Persekutuan (Rancangan FELDA) (Pindaan) 2025","vi":"Lệnh về Đường bộ liên bang (Chương trình FELDA) (Sửa đổi) năm 2025","th":"คำสั่งทางหลวงสหพันธ์ (โครงการ FELDA) (การแก้ไข) ค.ศ. 2025","id":"Perintah Jalan Raya Federal (Skema FELDA) (Perubahan) Tahun 2025"},"level":"regulation","category":"05_其他及未分类","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA42","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2025","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 3 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\05_其他及未分类\\2025_P.U.(A)42-2025_FEDERAL ROADS (FELDA SCHEME) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2025.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H5882-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Jalan Persekutuan\n\n(Skim Felda) (Pindaan) 2025.\n\n(2) Perintah ini mula berkuat kuasa pada 31 Januari 2025.\n\nPindaan Jadual Pertama"}},{"id":"MY-H5882-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Perintah Jalan Persekutuan (Skim Felda) 1991 [P.U. (A) 449/1991],\n\nyang disebut \"Perintah ibu\" dalam Perintah ini, dipinda dalam Jadual Pertama\n\ndi bawah kepala Negeri Melaka, berhubung dengan butiran Kemendore—\n\n(a) dalam ruang Nombor Laluan Bagi Jalan Masuk, dengan menggantikan\n\nperkataan \"—\" dengan perkataan \"1336\";\n\n(b) dalam ruang Jalan Masuk (km), dengan menggantikan perkataan \"2.479\"\n\ndengan perkataan \"2.150\"; dan\n\n(c) dalam ruang Jalan Kampung (km), dengan menggantikan perkataan\n\n\"6.559\" dengan perkataan \"7.886\".\n\nPindaan Jadual Kedua"}},{"id":"MY-H5882-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"ms":"3. Perintah ibu dipinda dalam Jadual Kedua dengan memasukkan selepas\n\nPETA 30: PALONG 16-TEMBANGAU (NEGERI SEMBILAN) peta yang berikut:\n\n\".\n\n\"PETA 31: KEMENDORE\n\nDibuat 24 Januari 2025\n\n[KKR.100-1/2/18; PN(PU2)391/JLD.51]\n\n DATO SRI ALEXANDER NANTA LINGGI\n\n Menteri Kerja Raya\n\n[Akan dibentangkan di Dewan Rakyat menurut seksyen 4 Akta Jalan Persekutuan 1959]\n\nFEDERAL ROADS ACT 1959\n\nFEDERAL ROADS (FELDA SCHEME) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2025\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 3 of the Federal Roads Act 1959\n\n[Act 376], the Minister, after consultation with the State Government of Malacca,\n\nmakes the following order:\n\nCitation and commencement"}}],"pack":"my-13"};
  FT["MY-H5883"] = {"id":"MY-H5883","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 42/2026&status=AMENDMENT","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2026年饲料（禁用抗生素、激素及其他化学品）（附表修正）条例","en":"FEED (PROHIBITED ANTIBIOTICS, HORMONES AND OTHER CHEMICALS) (AMENDMENT OF SCHEDULE) REGULATIONS 2026","orig":"FEED (PROHIBITED ANTIBIOTICS, HORMONES AND OTHER CHEMICALS) (AMENDMENT OF SCHEDULE) REGULATIONS 2026","ms":"Peraturan Makanan Ternak (Antibiotik, Hormon dan Bahan Kimia Lain yang Dilarang) (Pindaan Jadual) 2026","vi":"Quy định về Thức ăn chăn nuôi (Kháng sinh, hoóc-môn và hóa chất khác bị cấm) (Sửa đổi phụ lục) năm 2026","th":"ข้อบังคับอาหารสัตว์ (ยาปฏิชีวนะ ฮอร์โมน และสารเคมีอื่นที่ถูกห้าม) (การแก้ไขภาคผนวก) ค.ศ. 2026","id":"Peraturan Pakan Ternak (Antibiotik, Hormon dan Bahan Kimia Lain yang Dilarang) (Perubahan Lampiran) Tahun 2026"},"level":"regulation","category":"05_其他及未分类","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA42","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2026","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\05_其他及未分类\\2026_P.U.(A)42-2026_FEED (PROHIBITED ANTIBIOTICS, HORMONES AND OTHER CHEMICALS) (AMENDMENT OF SCHEDULE) REGULATIONS.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H5883-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. Peraturan-peraturan ini bolehlah dinamakan Peraturan-Peraturan Makanan\n\nHaiwan (Antibiotik, Hormon dan Bahan Kimia Lain Terlarang)\n\n(Pindaan Jadual) 2026.\n\nPindaan Jadual"}},{"id":"MY-H5883-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Peraturan-Peraturan Makanan Haiwan (Antibiotik, Hormon dan Bahan Kimia\n\nLain Terlarang) 2012 [P.U. (A) 272/2012] dipinda dalam Jadual dalam kepala\n\nA. Antibiotik, dalam ruang Antibiotik, dengan memasukkan selepas butiran (n)\n\nbutiran yang berikut:\n\nAntibiotik\n\n\"(o) Klortetrasiklin\n\n(p) Oksitetrasiklin\n\n(q) Amoksisilin\n\n(r) Ampisilin\n\n(s) Neomisin\n\n(t) Sefaleksin\n\n(u) Benzilpenisilin\n\n(v) Florfenikol\n\n(w) Norfloksasin\n\n(x) Tilmikosin\n\n(y) Tylvalosin\n\n(z) Spektinomisin\n\n(aa) Sulfamonometoksin\n\n(ab) Sulfadiazin\n\n(ac) Linkomisin\n\n(ad) Enramisin\n\n(ae) Basitrasin Metilen Disalisilat (BMD)\n\n(af) Apramisin\n\n(ag) Tiamulin\n\n(ah) Zink Basitrasin\n\n(ai) Trimethoprim\n\n(aj) Virginiamisin\"\n\nDibuat 9 Januari 2026\n\n[KP/LA/483/13 Jld.4; PN(PU2)702/IV]\n\nDATUK SERI HAJI MOHAMAD BIN SABU\n\nMenteri Pertanian dan Keterjaminan Makanan\n\n.\n\nFEED ACT 2009\n\nFEED (PROHIBITED ANTIBIOTICS, HORMONES AND OTHER CHEMICALS)\n\n(AMENDMENT OF SCHEDULE) REGULATIONS 2026\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by paragraph 53(2)(f) of the\n\nFeed Act 2009 [Act 698], the Minister, after consultation with the Board,\n\nmakes the following regulations:\n\nCitation"}}],"pack":"my-13"};
  FT["MY-H5884"] = {"id":"MY-H5884","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 430/2011&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":6,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2011年商品说明（清真定义）令","en":"TRADE DESCRIPTIONS (DEFINITION OF HALAL) ORDER 2011","orig":"TRADE DESCRIPTIONS (DEFINITION OF HALAL) ORDER 2011","ms":"Perintah Keterangan Perdagangan (Takrif Halal) 2011","vi":"Lệnh về Mô tả thương mại (Định nghĩa halal) năm 2011","th":"คำสั่งคำบรรยายสินค้า (นิยามของฮาลาล) ค.ศ. 2011","id":"Perintah Keterangan Dagang (Definisi Halal) Tahun 2011"},"level":"regulation","category":"02_民商事与经济法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA430","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2011","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 6 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\02_民商事与经济法\\2011_P.U.(A)430-2011_TRADE DESCRIPTIONS (DEFINITION OF HALAL) ORDER 2011.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H5884-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Perihal Dagangan\n(Takrif Halal) 2011.\n(2) Perintah ini mula berkuat kuasa pada 1 Januari 2012.\nTafsiran"}},{"id":"MY-H5884-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Dalam Perintah ini—\n\"Hukum Syarak\" ertinya undang -undang Islam mengikut Mazhab S yafii, atau\nundang-undang Islam dalam mana -mana satu daripada Mazhab lain sama ada Hanafi,\nMaliki atau Hambali yang telah dipersetujui oleh Yang Di -Pertuan Agong untuk\ndikuatkuasakan di Wilayah Persekutuan Kuala Lumpur, Labuan dan Putrajaya , Pulau\nPinang, Melaka, Sabah dan Sarawak atau oleh Raja bagi mana -mana Negeri untuk\ndikuatkuasakan di Negeri masing-masing;\n\"makanan\" termasuklah tiap -tiap barang yang dikilangkan, dij ual atau\ndigambarkan untuk digunakan sebagai makanan atau minuman bagi kegunaan manusia\natau yang memasuki ke dalam atau digunakan di dalam komposisi, penyediaan,\npengawetan, mana-mana makanan atau minuman bagi kegunaan manusia dan\ntermasuklah konfeksi, ba han kunyahan dan apa -apa bahan bagi makanan, minuman,\nkonfeksi atau bahan kunyahan itu;\n\"perkhidmatan yang berkaitan dengan makanan atau barang -barang\"\ntermasuklah  pengangkutan,  penyimpanan dan pemprosesan bahan mentah, penyajian\ndan peruncitan makanan atau barang-barang tersebut.\n\nHalal dan ungkapan lain ditakrifkan"}},{"id":"MY-H5884-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"ms":"3. (1) Apabila suatu makanan atau barang -barang diperihalkan sebagai halal\natau diperihalkan dengan apa -apa ungkapan lain untuk menunjukkan makanan atau\nbarang-barang itu boleh dimak an atau digunakan oleh orang Islam, ungkapan tersebut\nbererti makanan atau barang-barang itu:\n(a) bukanlah dan tidaklah terdiri daripada atau mengandungi apa -apa\nbahagian atau benda daripada binatang yang dilarang oleh Hukum\nSyarak bagi orang Islam untuk memakannya atau yang tidak\ndisembelih mengikut Hukum Syarak;\n(b) tidak mengandungi apa-apa benda yang najis mengikut Hukum\nSyarak;\n(c) tidak memabukkan mengikut Hukum  Syarak;\n(d) tidak mengandungi mana -mana bahagian anggota manusia atau\nhasilan daripadanya yang tidak dibenarkan oleh Hukum Syarak;\n(e) tidak beracun atau memudaratkan kesihatan;\n(f) tidak disediakan, diproses atau dikilang menggunakan apa-apa\nperalatan yang dicemari najis mengikut Hukum Syarak; dan\n(g) tidaklah dalam masa menyediakan, memproses atau\nmenyimpannya bersentuhan, bercampur atau berdekatan dengan\napa-apa makanan yang gagal memenuhi perenggan (a) dan (b).\n(2) Apabila perkhidmatan yang berhubung dengan makanan atau\nbarang-barang diperihalkan sebagai halal atau diperihalkan dengan apa -apa ungkapan\nlain untuk menunjukkan perkhidmatan itu boleh digunakan oleh orang Islam, ungkapan\ntersebut bererti perkhidmatan yang berhubung dengan makanan atau barang -barang\nitu dijalankan mengikut Hukum Syarak.\n\n(3) Mana-mana orang yang membekalkan atau menawar kan untuk\nmembekalkan apa -apa makanan, barang -barang atau perkhidmatan yang berhubung\ndengan makanan atau barang -barang itu yang diperihalkan sebagai halal atau\ndiperihalkan dengan apa -apa ungkapan lain yang bertentangan dengan perenggan ini\nadalah melakukan suatu kesalahan.\nKesalahan bagi memperdayakan atau mengelirukan"}},{"id":"MY-H5884-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"ms":"4. (1) Mana-mana orang yang membekalkan atau menawar kan untuk\nmembekalkan apa-apa makanan dengan membuat apa-apa representasi atau perbuatan\nyang boleh memperdayakan atau mengelirukan mana-mana orang bahawa makanan itu\nadalah halal atau boleh dimakan oleh orang Islam adalah melakukan suatu kesalahan.\n(2) Bagi maksud subperenggan (1), \"representasi atau perbuatan \" termasuklah\npenggunaan ayat-ayat suci Al -Quran atau apa -apa perkara atau objek yang berhubung\ndengan agama Islam sama ada di premis di mana makanan itu dijual atau di bekas di\nmana makanan itu dibekalkan.\n(3) Jika mana -mana orang dipertuduh dengan suatu kesalahan di bawah\nsubperenggan (1), beban untuk membuktikan bahawa makanan yang dibekalkan atau\nditawar untuk dibekalkan adalah halal mengikut kehendak perenggan 3 hendaklah\nterletak pada orang yang dipertuduh itu.\nPenalti"}},{"id":"MY-H5884-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"ms":"5. Mana-mana orang yang melakukan kesalahan di bawah Perintah ini boleh,\napabila disabitkan—\n(a) jika orang itu ialah suatu pertubuhan perbadanan, didenda tidak melebihi\nlima juta ringgit , dan bagi kesalahan yang kedua atau yang berikutnya ,\ndidenda tidak melebihi sepuluh juta ringgit; atau\n(b) jika orang itu bukan suatu pertubuhan perbadanan, didenda tidak\nmelebihi satu juta ringgit atau dipenjarakan selama tempoh tidak\nmelebihi tiga tahun atau kedua -duanya, dan bagi kesal ahan yang kedua\n\natau yang berikutnya , didenda tidak melebihi lima juta ringgit atau\ndipenjarakan selama tempoh tidak melebihi lima tahun atau kedua -\nduanya.\nPembatalan"}},{"id":"MY-H5884-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6"},"text":{"ms":"6. Perintah Perihal Dagangan (Penggunaan Perbahasan \"Halal\") 1975\n[P.U. (A) 237/1975] dibatalkan.\nDibuat 29 Disember 2011\n[KPDN(PUU)(PU2)26/5/5; PN(PU2)120/VI]\nDATO' SERI AHMAD HUSNI MOHAMAD HANADZLAH\nMenteri Kewangan Kedua\nyang menjalankan fungsi-fungsi Menteri Perdagangan Dalam\nNegeri, Koperasi dan Kepenggunaan\n\nTRADE DESCRIPTIONS ACT 2011\nTRADE DESCRIPTIONS (DEFINITION OF HALAL) ORDER 2011\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 28 of the Trade Descriptions Act 2011\n[Act 730], the Minister makes the following order:\nCitation and commencement"}}],"pack":"my-13"};
  FT["MY-H5885"] = {"id":"MY-H5885","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 430/2012&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2012年关税（计价）（棕榈油）（第49号）令","en":"CUSTOMS (VALUES) (PALM OIL) (NO. 49) ORDER 2012","orig":"CUSTOMS (VALUES) (PALM OIL) (NO. 49) ORDER 2012","ms":"Perintah Kastam (Nilai) (Minyak Sawit) (Bilangan 49) 2012","vi":"Lệnh về Hải quan (Trị giá) (Dầu cọ) (số 49) năm 2012","th":"คำสั่งศุลกากร (มูลค่า) (น้ำมันปาล์ม) (ฉบับที่ 49) ค.ศ. 2012","id":"Perintah Kepabeanan (Nilai) (Minyak Kelapa Sawit) (Nomor 49) Tahun 2012"},"level":"regulation","category":"03_涉外投资与贸易","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA430","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2012","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\03_涉外投资与贸易\\2012_P.U.(A)430-2012_CUSTOMS (VALUES) (PALM OIL) (NO. 49) ORDER 2012.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H5885-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Kastam (Nilai -Nilai)\n(Minyak Kelapa Sawit) (No. 49) 2012 dan hendaklah mula berkuat kuasa bagi tempoh\ndari 3 Disember 2012 hingga 9 Disember 2012.\n\nPemungutan dan pembayaran duti kastam"}},{"id":"MY-H5885-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Bagi maksud pemungutan dan pembayaran duti -duti kastam, menurut\nperuntukan-peruntukan Perintah Duti Kastam 2007 [ P.U. (A) 441/2007], nilai bagi tiap -\ntiap satu barang be rduti yang dinyatakan dalam ruang (1) dan (2) Jadual mengikut\nunitnya yang tersebut dalam ruang (3) hendaklah nilai yang dinyatakan dalam\nruang (4).\n\nCUSTOMS ACT 1967\n\nCUSTOMS (VALUES) (PALM OIL) (NO. 49) ORDER 2012\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 12 of the Customs Act 1967 [Act 235], the\nMinister makes the following order:\n\nCitation and commencement\n\nJADUAL/SCHEDULE\nBarang\n(Goods)\n(1)\n\nSubkepala\n(Subheading)\n(2)\nUnit\n(Unit)\n(3)\nNilai\n(Value)\n(4)\nCrude Palm Oil 1511.10 100 tonne RM2,151.67\n\nDibuat    30 November  2012\nMade      30  November  2012\n[KE.HT(94)819/03-6/KLT. 11(60); Perb.(8.20)116/1-4; PN(G)168/VII]\n\n          Dengan arahan Menteri Kewangan/\n          By direction of the Minister of Finance\n\n    Bagi pihak dan atas nama Menteri Kewangan/\n          On behalf and in the name of the Minister of Finance\n\n DATO' SITI HALIMAH BINTI ISMAIL\n     Setiausaha/\nUnder Secretary\nBahagian Analisa Cukai/\nTax Analysis Division"}}],"pack":"my-13"};
